N2  - Three dimensional character acquisition of complicated facial modality is needed in clinical environment, and multi-characteristic variables need to be analyzed according to statistics methods. Three-dimensional (3D) face acquisition and three-dimensional character selection method based on reverse engineering is proposed in this article. Three-dimensional facial data of thirty undergraduates was used to classify 3D face of four characteristic variables. K-Means Cluster Analysis of Statistics and analyses was used to determine the number of the group. Discriminant analysis was used to structure the function of each group so as to determine the classification of random face. Results showed that the precision of 3D face acquisition was 0.02-0.2 mm with the method of this paper, and 3D face could be statistical analyzed. The model of this paper is a useful method for face plastic surgery, facial paralysis, facial surgical evaluation and rehabilitation design.
