N2  - Conjunctivodacryocystorhinostomy with Jones tube placement is a procedure primarily performed for the correction of symptomatic epiphora caused by severe stenosis or obstruction of both upper and lower canaliculi. A Pyrex glass tube (Jones tube) is positioned at the caruncle extending into the middle meatus of the nose, thus creating a new outflow pathway for tears to enter the nose. Recently, the endoscopic route has gained popularity and may confer advantages over the traditional external route, including lack of a cutaneous scar, faster operative times, and decreased blood loss. This article describes our endoscopic approach to Jones tube placement, which we have found to be safe, reliable, and well tolerated by the patient. © 2008 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.
