N2  - Objective: Using functional magnetic resonance imaging (fMRI) to study the brain response changes in Hegu acupoint of peripheral facial paralysis by electroacupuncture (EA), and tried to research the mechanism of acupuncture and the function essence of acupoint and reveal function mechanism of puncture from the angle of neurology and brain science we wanted to have an energetic effect on clinical application and modernization of acupuncture and moxibustion. Methods: Six patients with peripheral facial paralysis on the left were screened. Hegu acupoint on the left were acupunctured, functional MRI data were obtained from scanning the whole brain at the same time. Acquired functional data were processed by SPM software and functional responses were established by t-test analysis (P<0.05). Results: Electroacupuncture (EA) hegu on the left induced signal decreases of left cingulate gyrus, bilateral middle frontal gyrus, right middle occipital gyrus; induced signal increases of left postcentral gyrus, right inferior frontal gyrus, right superior temporal gyrus, right insula, left precentral gyrus. Conclusion: There exists some correlation between acupoints stimulation and encephalic region. During Hegu acupoint EA on the left, multi-encephalic regions signal appeared changes and the influenced area is intinately correlated to the effect and indication of acupoint.
