N2  - Cartilage-hair hypoplasia is a rare, autosomal recessive primary immunodeficiency disorder characterized by predominantly T-cell deficiency and metaphyseal chondrodysplasia. The authors summarize current knowledge on molecular genetics, diagnostic characteristics and therapeutic options of this inherited immunodeficiency.
