N2  - The facial palsy (FP) is the most frequent cranial neuropathy. FP not only disturb eating or drinking, it's an important social problem, because our face is one of the most important elements in social communication. Although the most frequent etiology of facial palsy is a frigore o idiopathic, the FC could be the expression or consequences of several diseases that have an specific treatment. In this article we analyze FP from embryological, anatomical and semiological point of view.
