N2  - Aim: Conventional rehabilitation evaluation cannot provide the objective data for analysis. In the whole therapy of facial palsy, monitoring software can periodically monitor the facial movement change of facial paralytics and create real-time evaluation archives for assistant diagnosis of facial neural palsy. Methods: The monitoring rehabilitation software of facial paralysis is developed independently under Visual Basic 6.0 environment. It can gather both video and photos at dynamic and static states. According to the symmetry of face and rules of facial movement, it chooses some feature points of five organs such as eyes, mouth and tongue to describe facial movement track, then compute the feature parameters, which include moving distance, speed, acceleration and slope of angulus oris or canthus. The software also creates an objective data archives for facial paralytic by the parameters selected in the process of moving. Results: The monitor software records measurement results, including moving distance, average speed, maximum speed, average acceleration, maximum acceleration and so on. The change trend of feature parameters during the process assists to diagnose the rehabilitation of facial neural palsy patients. Therefore, the monitoring software can offer an objective and simple analyzing tool for doctors to improve the treatment scheme. Conclusion: The monitor software is an innovation in the monitoring rehabilitation of the facial nerve function after facial neural palsy. It can replace the traditional rehabilitation evaluation methods that focus on the subjective evaluation, and reflect the rehabilitation of facial paralytics objectively.
