N2  - The lips are important facial structure with crucial importance both functionally and cosmetically. Its flexible structure facilitates contribution to uniquely important functions like smiling, talking, eating and drinking. If swelling develops in one or both lips it hinders these functions as well as it may disturb the affected person psychologically. Many pathological conditions are associated with lip swelling. Some are acute, while many are chronic. Some conditions present with diffuse lip swelling like orofacial granulomatosis whereas others start as localized ulcers or erosions that may progress into diffuse lip swelling because of edema like traumatic ulcers, erythema multiforme or neoplasms like squamous cell carcinoma. In this review some important causes of lip swelling are discussed.
