N2  - Rectal adenocarcinoma may spread to the central nervous system and may result in various symptomatologies. Rectal adenocarcinoma presenting with multiple cranial nerve palsies has not been reported. A case of metastatic rectal adenocarcinoma with audio-visual complaints is presented. The therapeutic approach is discussed briefly. It is concluded that multiple cranial nerve palsies in a case with rectal adenocarcinoma herald brainstem metastasis, high risk of sudden death and need for immediate intervention appropriately.
