N2  - Base of skull fractures after Head trauma is a common problem. Management is often conservative. Trauma surgeons should be familiar with the clinical signs, appropriate imaging and guidelines for referral to neurosurgery. We review the current evidence on antibiotic use. Recognition and management of the immediate and delayed complications of skull base fractures is discussed. © SAGE Publications 2007.
