N2  - The paper deals with various etiologies, clinical symptoms and the differential diagnosis of paresis nervi facialis peripherica, particularly of the central type. In connection with the above, the clinical syptoms justifying the diagnosis of Ramsey-Hunt syndrome, Mobius syndrome and the familial-hereditary Melkersson-Rosenthal syndrome are presented. The diagnosic work-up aimed at establishing the causes and appropriate methods of treatment of the condition are also discused. © 2007 by Polskie Towarzystwo Pediatryczne.
