N2  - The incidence of extracranial and intracranial complications of COM and cholesteatoma has decreased since the proliferation of antibiotics early in the twentieth century. However, these complications continue to occur, and can be lethal if they are not identified and treated properly. Therapy for the complications associated with COM, unlike those of AOM, usually includes surgical intervention, in addition to medical therapy. As medical (antibiotic) therapy continues to improve, and new imaging techniques are introduced, less invasive treatment modalities may be shown to be as effective as the classic, time-tested, surgical options. © 2006 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.
