N2  - The Plasma cell mucositis in an heterogeneous group of clinical manifestations, commonly characterized by plasma cell infiltrate under the epithelium structures. The illness can involve a singular anatomical region or represents the epiphenomenon of rather and complex cases syndrome like a Meischer or Melkersson-Rosenthal syndrome. The anatomical localization and extension are the responsible parameters of the different clinical presentation of the pathology. In this work the Authors give a review of scientific literature about the theme and describe a typical case of Melkersson-Rosenthal syndrome in a 16 years old female treated by double therapeutic approach (surgical and pharmacological devices) and a Zoon's balanitis in a 65 years old man treated by laser.
