N2  - We reported a clinical study of 54 patients (51 males and 3 females) with Warthin's tumor treated in our hospital from 1999 to 2005. The accuracy for diagnosis of Warthin's tumor with fine needle aspiration (FNA) and 99mTc scintigraphy were 64.8% and 82.9%. Temporary facial nerve palsy after the operation occurred in 11 patients. The period until recovering was 5.9 weeks on the average. A significant difference neither the age or the operation time or the tumor size was admitted in the facial nerve palsy. The surgery for tumors in deep lobe was suggested that it was necessary to be done carefully.
