N2  - Objective: To probe into the opportunity for acupuncture and moxibustion in the treatment of peripheral facial paralysis. Data Sources: A computer-based online research of Chinese papers about opportunity for acupuncture and moxibustion in the treatment of peripheral facial paralysis published from January 1994 to May 2006 was conducted for 5 times in CNKI with the key words of "Peripheral facial paralysis" and "acupuncture and moxibustion" combined with "opportunity", "stages", "acute stage","rehabilitation stage","residual stage"respectively. Study Selection: Papers about opportunity for acupuncture and moxibustion in the treatment of peripheral facial paralysis were selected in the first searching. Inclusive criteria: 1 Research on acupuncture and moxibustion in the treatment of peripheral facial paralysis. 2 Research on comparison in peripheral facial paralysis among different stages. 3 Viewpoints of acupuncture and moxibustion in the treatment of peripheral facial paralysis in different stage. Data Extraction: Over 173 literatures were screened, and a total of 28 studies were involved in the analysis of results. Data Synthesis: Twenty-eight papers mainly represented that the therapy of acupuncture and moxibustion should be applied in treating peripheral facial paralysis of acute stage as soon as possible. The acupuncture in acute stage should be performed as less acupoints, light excitation and short time of retention in treatment by combining with TDP or moxibustion without electroacupuncture or light-stimulation electroacupuncture. While in the rehabilitation stage, deep insertation, strong manipulation, more acupoints and penetration acupuncture or electroacupuncture should be adopted. Tonifying method, strong excitation and exsanguination of collaterals in region were performed in residual stage. Conclusion: The clinical effect on peripheral facial paralysis will be enhanced by using acupuncture and moxibustion therapy corresponding to the different stage of the disease.
