N2  - Facial paralysis is not uncommon in patients with severe craneofacial trauma. Sometimes is difficult to make an accurate diagnosis and locate the lesion. In this paper we review the problem from both the ethiological and the mechanism point of view responsible of the neural lesion. We make some practical considerations in evaluating and diagnosing the facial paralysis. We also describe the different treatment modalities and surgical indications.
