N2  - Ramsay Hunt syndrome is rare among children. It has been reported that the frequency of this syndrome among all of the pediatric facial paresis cases is 0.5-10.5% in infants and toddler and 3.7-24.4% in school-age-children, respectively. Although prognosis of this syndrome in children is better than that in adults, the treatment is still controversial. We obtained satisfactory results in the treatment of three cases of Ramsay Hunt syndrome in children by administeration of acyclovir and predonisolone.
