N2  - Amphiphysin, a synaptic vesicle protein, is an auto-immune target in rare cases of paraneoplastic neurological disorders. We report two additional cases with distinct neurological syndromes and paraneoplastic anti-amphiphysin antibodies. The first patient, a 59-year-old man, presented with cerebellar and cranial nerve dysfunction and small cell lung carcinoma. The second, a 77-year-old woman, presented with left brachial plexopathy followed by sensorimotor neuropathy and breast carcinoma. Copyright © 2006 S. Karger AG.
