N2  - Aim: To observe the clinical effect of huangjiao granule combined with stroke unit on patients with acute cerebral infarction in heat phlegm fu-organ syndrome as compared with routine treatment in neurological department. Methods: Patients with acute cerebral infarction in heat phlegm fu-organ syndrome were selected from Neurological Department of Wuhan Hospital of Integrated Traditional Chinese Medicine and Western Medicine between October 2001 and March 2003. All patients were diagnosed with Diagnosed Criteria of Cerebral Infarction which was set by the Second Cerebrovascular Disease Academic Conference of China and Clinical Research Criteria on Treating Stroke by Chinese Herbs which was set by Ministry of Health of the People's Republic of China in October 1993. Totally 103 patients were regarded as control group from October 2001 to March 2002, and 120 patients were regarded as observational group from October 2002 to March 2003. Patients in control group were treated with routine treatment in neurological department for 21 days, but patients in observational group were taken 10 g huangjiao granule orally (consisted of raw rhubarb and buffalo horn, provided by Preparation Room of Wuhan Hospital of Combination of Traditional Chinese Medicine and Western Medicine, batch number: 021120) for 3 times a day. After vital sings were stable, patients were treated with language rehabilitation training and physical rehabilitation training for 21 days. Then indexes of patients in both groups were observed before and after treatment, including scores of neurological impairment, cases of language, facial paralysis and functional impairment of muscles of upper and lower limbs, cases of Barthel index in activity of daily living (ADL), clinical effect and cases of singultus and constipation. Results: Totally 120 patients in observational group and 103 patients in control group entered the final analysis without any loss. 1 Scores of neurological impairment in both groups were decreased after treatment as compared with those before treatment (20.8±5.6, 27.2±11.5; 24.3±8.2, 28.1±13.2; t=5.078, 2.482, P < 0.01-0.05), and those in observational group were lower than those in control group (t=3.577, P < 0.01). 2 Symptoms of facial paralysis, language and muscle of upper and lower limbs were improved remarkably after treatment, especially improvements in observational group were superior to those in control group (P < 0.05). 3 Cases of Barthel index in ADL were more in observational group than those in control group (x2=8.71, P < 0.01). 4 Recovery rate of patients in observational group was higher than that in control group, but deteriorated and recent death rates were lower than those in control group, and there was significant difference (P < 0.05). 5 There were significant differences between observational group and control group on the aspect of singultus and constipation diagnosed with x2 test after treatment (5, 10; 11, 28; x2 =4.77, 12.47, P < 0.05). Conclusion: Huangjiao granule combined with stroke unit can improve ability of ADL, decrease neurological impairment and improve symptoms of singultus and constipation of patients with acute cerebral infarction in heat phlegm fu-organ syndrome.
