N2  - The last two decades have witnessed remarkable improvement in delineating the pathogenesis of vascular anomalies. Improved definitions based on this genetic-anatomic-histologic classification have allowed the development of multidisciplinary approaches toward disease treatment and management. As our appreciation of the embryonic and developmental contributions to disease increases, so does our ability to develop novel strategies for management of previously insurmountably complex lesions. Molecular and pharmacologic manipulation of vascular anomalies holds great promise. © 2006 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.
