N2  - The case of 65-year male patient with an stage T4, mucoepidermoid carcinoma of the parotid gland is presented. The tumor of this patient was classified as a tumor of high grade of malignancy in according to the Goode classification. The patient received surgical treatment and radiotherapy. After 10 months, the patient has remained asymptomatic, with a permanent facial palsy as complication of the treatment. The absence of regional and distant metastasis was peculiar in this patient. The clinical aspects, the diagnosis and the applied treatment were discussed, as soon as the frequency in other places of the world.
