N2  - Non-ablative remodeling has been proposed as a new and safety anti-ageing treatment. The objective of this study was to evaluate the efficacy and safety of non ablative skin remodeling with a 1540 nm Er:Glass laser and to evaluate the motivation of people for this type of treatment. 36 patients have a mean of 3 treatments every month provided by 9 dermatologists. A hemi-face was treated, the other was used as control. We evaluated with a questionnary the subjective effects, the safety of this treatment but also the motivation of the patients. Photographies were done and we also collected the doctors impressions with this laser. Only 32 patients were evaluated. Only 50% had good or mild results. Almost both patients and laserists thought that even if this laser is probably interesting for anti ageing prevention, its efficiency is insufficient for the dermatologists practice in the private exercise. © Nouv. Dermatol. 2006.
