N2  - Moebius syndrome is a rare congenital disorder with the primary diagnostic criteria of congenital facial diplegia and abducent nerve palsy. Orofacial anomalies and limb malformations may be associated with the disorder. We report a family (father and two sons) with a subset of the Moebius syndrome.
