N2  - The successful treatment of GH deficiency with rhGH has tended to dominate clinical and research activities related to growth disorders. In the last 15 years, the development of the molecular investigation of the GH-IGF-I axis and the availability of rhIGF-I has renewed interest in the field of disorders characterized by GH insensitivity. Important advances have been made in both the understanding of the physiology of this axis, which is pivotal for normal human growth, and the potential for the therapeutic use of rhIGF-I. This article highlights the principal developments to diagnosis and treatment of this fascinating group of human disorders. © 2005 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.
