N2  - We investigated the usefulness of manipulative physiotherapy as a means of rehabilitation for patients with Bell's palsy. Of 24 patients diagnosed as having Bell's palsy, 12 were treated with low frequency therapy alone and 12 were treated with a combination of low frequency therapy and manipulative physiotherapy. The length of time required until healing did not differ significantly between the two groups. However, in the low frequency therapy + manipulative physiotherapy group, 7 patients recovered within 3 weeks of the start of treatment, but none of the patients treated with low frequency therapy alone recovered within 3 weeks. Manipulative physiotherapy was found to be useful in shortening the time required for recovery from Bell's palsy.
