N2  - To investigate the surgical treatment of peripheral facial nerve paralysis as well as the factors which affect the operation effect. Fifty-one cases of peripheral facial nerve paracusis were analyzed retrospectively. Forty-two cases were followed up. Among them, twenty-two cases who received facial nerve decompression reached House I-II degree (22/36), 2 cases facial nerve anastomosis reached House I-II degree (2/4), and the function recovery of 2 cases who received facial nerve grafting > III degree both. Intensive and timely surgery is an efficient way in treating of peripheral facial nerve paralysis.
