N2  - When the differential diagnosis could include Lyme disease, careful history and a strong suspicion can often be key to a correct diagnosis, particularly in patients with atypical presentations. We report the case of a patient presenting with multiple cranial neuropathy whose diagnosis of Lyme disease was confirmed by travel history, MRI, and immunologic testing.
