N2  - We present two patients with Guillain-Barré syndrome. They were admitted at the hospital with facial paralysis, an uncommon form of presentation. The diagnosis was confirmed by electrophysiologic study. The treatment administrated was plasmapheresis and intravenous immune-globulin, and the two patients had significant improvement.
