N2  - Objective: To review the application status of the methods of acupuncture, external treatment, drugs, and rehabilitation, etc. on facial paralysis so as to get the more effective treatment methods. Data sources: Using the key terms "facial paralysis, treatment", we searched the Chinese journals full-text database and Wanfang database from January 1994 to January 2004 in Chinese. Study selection: Totally 62 articles on facial paralysis treatment in which the original references included the methods of acupuncture, external treatment, drugs, and rehabilitation and so on. Data extraction: Seventeen out of the 62 articles were excluded because of duplicated summarizations, the, other 45 articles were sorted for review and 26 articles for references. Data synthesis: Facial paralysis was often induced by acute nonsuppurative inflammation occurred in facial nerve. In the treatment of facial paralysis, the combination of traditional Chinese medicine and western medicine was used mostly, acupuncture and drugs was a large part. Each method was effective for promoting the functional rehabilitation of muscle; moreover, the effect of combination method was obvious. Conclusion: The combination of traditional Chinese medicine and western medicine can promote the functional rehabilitation of nerve and muscle, reduce the sequels; It is valuable to guide the idea for adopting the combination of traditional Chinese medicine and western medicine for facial paralysis.
