N2  - Following subjects are presented: General ENT: tonsillectomy, predictive factors for post-tonsillectomy hemorrage, oxymetry, sleeping breathing problems on developpement of the child, consens on otitis media with effusion. Rhinology: reflux in chronic sinusitis, importance of olfaction, consens on chronic rhinosinusitis in terms of definition, diagnosis, epidemiology, and treatment, role of adenoids in chronic sinusitis. Otology: postraumatic and idiopathic cupulolithiasis, mastoidectomy, dose limited gamma knife in the treatment of neurinomas, treatment of tinnitus, treatment of otitis externa. Salivary glands: Coxackie virus as cause of Sjögren syndrome, Botox in hypersalivation, cortisone in facial palsy, Bell's palsy in nasal flu vaccine. Diverse: thyroidectomies, endoscopic thyroidectomies, interest of the ligasure.
