N2  - The osteodysplasia of the temporal bone can produce many different symptoms like involvement restrict to the temporal bone or with impairment of others bone. We consider, in this study, two entity like rare osteodysplasia that are the osteopetrosis and the Camurati-Engelmann's disease, last one extremely rare. We present two cases of osteopetrosis, in the benign form (Albers-Schulenburg's disease), a patient of 11 years old and another of 48 years old, both male and a patient of 28 years old, female, with the Camurati-Engelmann's disease. The facial palsy was a manifestation in two of the patients. We discuss some aspects about the clinical manifestations, radiologic findings, as well as the differential diagnostic and the therapy in the face of the complications of the diseases.
