N2  - Airway obstruction in children with craniofacial abnormalities can cause significant morbidity and mortality. The status of the airway should be assessed as part of the initial and follow-up clinical evaluations. When abnormalities exist, an approach to effective management can follow rational and effective guidelines. © 2004 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.
