N2  - The hemifacial spasm is an involuntary paroxistic contraction of the facial muscle, appears more frecuently in the left side and in females and seldom disapears by itself. Has being treated with botulin infections with poor results. We present 116 decompressions that were done to 88 patients in a 10 years period 1992-2002. All patients had previous medical treatment. They were operated with microsurgical technique and were followed from 1 to 133 months. The results we excellent in 70.45 % after the first operation, good in 6.82% and poor in 20.45%. At the final long observation were excellent in 81.82% good in 6.82 % and poor in 11.36%. The main complications were hipoacusia and transitory facial paresis. We believe that the surgical treatment is the best option for this condition. ©INNN, 2004.
