N2  - Although the classic symptom of Lyme disease is the erythema migrans rash, the diagnosis is often confused because symptoms may be those of a generalized flu-like illness or may affect various body systems (eg, acute and late neuroborreliosis, Lyme carditis, and Lyme arthritis). All tests are confirmatory; but testing is not standardized and there is often confusion over interpretation of results. Primary care physicians can successfully treat most patients who have Lyme disease, often with a 2- to 3-week course of oral antibiotics.
