N2  - We present the case of an immunocompetent man who presented with multiple and progressive cranial nerve palsies. The cause was found to be aspergillosis of the petrous bone, arising as a result of chronic fungal otitis media. Despite treatment with local excision and systemic anti-fungal therapy, he died after suffering a subarachnoid haemorrhage. Diagnosis rests upon prompt radiological imaging and the acquisition of tissue for histological examination and culture but cannot be made without awareness of the condition. © British Geriatrics Society 2004; all rights reserved.
