N2  - The peripheral facial paralysis is a disease which attacks individuals in all ages, being frequent in usual medical practice, and may cause emotional, social and professional changes because of the sequels that occur up to 30% of the cases. We present the anatomic aspects, clinical findings, complementary tests and the treatment of the several etiologies, that must be known by all physicians to avoid so, the sequels caused by this disease.
