N2  - A 1.5-month-old female developed a growing mass in the left parotid gland with facial nerve palsy. The patient underwent a superficial parotidectomy with preservation of the facial nerve. The pathologic diagnosis was infantile hemangioendothelioma. After the operation, her face was paralized for a month and completely recovered. No recurrence of the parotid tumor was observed for 6 years.
