N2  - A 60-year-old female with HAM developed bilateral facial palsy. Right facial palsy developed and improved in two weeks. Prickling pain on chest and infrascapular region of the left side appeared and left facial palsy developed. Chest hyperesthesia, dysuria, dizziness and finger tremor followed it. HTLV-I was observed in her whole blood. She was diagnosed with HAM, and prednisolone was administered. After the medication, these symptoms were improved. Left facial palsy improved in 4 months. We suspected that HTLV-I infection was related to the onset of facial palsy.
