N2  - The management of patients with cerebellopontine angle (CPA) or internal auditory canal (IAC) lesions is presented from the surgical and radiation oncology perspective. A full appreciation of the treatment options these patients experience is important so that their pre- and post-operative imaging exams may be understood and interpreted correctly. This article discusses in detail the clinical management of these patients. © 2003 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.
