N2  - Cyclosporine was suggested recently by Japanese workers to provoke central nervous systems symptoms in Behcet's disease. We report 2 cases supporting this notion. Our aim is to draw the attention of physicians to such phenomenon as cyclosporine being frequently advocated in the treatment of uveitis due to Behcet's disease.
