N2  - The authors investigated 130 patients with herpes zoster. They confirmed its more frequent incidence in patients above the age of 60 years. The most frequent site (34.6%) was the innervation area of thoracic nerves and the area of the trigeminal nerve (27.7%). They recorded 24.6% complications associated directly with herpes zoster. Ramsay-Hunt's syndrome was recorded in three subjects. They did not observe neuralgias in child patients and in patients with malignant tumours. During hospitalization they administered to 128 (98.5%) patients acyclovir by the i.v. route, to 27.3% longer than 5 days, with a favourable therapeutic effect, without undesirable side-effects.
