N2  - Postherpetic neuralgia is an independent morbidity unit representing the complication of acute infection herpes zoster. Postherpetic neuralgia is based on abnormal sensitive-motoric junctions of peripheral and central nervous system. It is of chronic character that does not often respond even to combined analgesic treatment. In her paper the author analyzes the problems of infection reactivation of infection, clinical course of the disease and modes of prevention and treatment of postherpetic neuralgia represented mainly by causal antiviral therapy.
