N2  - This study determined the pathogenic potential of Staphylococcus epidermidis. Ninety-one isolates from patients with infectious keratitis and 38 from controls were studied for slime production. Thirty-six ulcer isolates (39.5%) and 6 controls (15.7%) were slime positive. Significantly more slime-positive strains were isolated from patients with moderate to severe degrees of ulcerative keratitis than from controls. Keratitis induced in rabbits also showed that slime-positive organisms produced the severe form of ulcerative lesions.
