N2  - Objectives: Previous studies suggested an alteration of Eustachian tube function due to an impairment of parasympathetic mucosal innervation. Methods: For this reason, the 'tubal opening pressure', 'tissue resistance pressure' and the 'positive' and 'negative residual pressure' were measured in 20 patients with peripheral idiopathic facial nerve palsy in a pressure chamber using the dual-impedance method described by Münker. Results: The data of the unaffected side did not vary significantly from those of the paralyzed side. Conclusion: It is supposed that alterations of the secretion layer in the distal part of the Eustachian tube have no notable influence on the Eustachian tube opening and closing. Copyright © 2003 S. Karger AG, Basel.
