N2  - Four children, aged one to two years with acute mastoiditis are reported. They were treated at the Department of Otorhinolaryngology, Nakagami Hospital from 1999 to 2000. All patients had otalgia, postauricular swelling and high fever, but there were no intracranial complications such as facial paralysis, meningitis. All patients were treated with intravenous antibiotic therapy and myringotomy. But mastoidectomy was not perfomed in any of the patients.
