N2  - Objective: To study the evaluation value of blink reflex (BR) in early peripheral facial palsy within 3 days from onset. Method: 60 healthy people and 32 cases of early facial palsy were tested with BR.. All cases were followed up until the 6th month. Result: We obtained BR normal values. The patients showed absent response, delayed latency or irregular response on the paretic side. The BR manifestations were correlated to the function of facial nerve. The cases with presence of BR response within 3 days recovered satisfactorily in 6 months. But only some of the cases with absence BR response had a bad outcome. Conclusion: BR is a very sensitive electrodiagnostic test to facial palsy. BR results can react the abnormality degree of facial nerve within 3 days of onset and it's also useful to predict the prognosis.
