N2  - Salivary duct carcinomas are an uncommon but distinct group of highly malignant salivary gland tumours. They often carry a poor prognosis unless discovered early and managed aggressively with primary tumour resection, cervical neck dissection and radiotherapy. We report an unusual case of undiagnosed salivary duct carcinoma with a three-year-old facial nerve paralysis and endocranial metastases, revealed by its cutaneous involvement.
