N2  - A seventeen-year-old male presented with migratory oro-facial swelling. There was no history of facial paralysis or any abnormality of the tongue, detected. All laboratory investigations were normal. Despite the absence of classical triad, diagnosis of Melkersson-Rosenthal syndrome was made after histopathology. The diagnostic dilemma in such atypical cases is beingdiscussed. The role of serratiopeptidase in this syndrome looks promising.
