N2  - A case of Rhabdomyosarcoma of middle ear and mastoid with secondaries in the temporal lobe and cerebellum and facial palsy in a 16 year old male patient is reported. The patient presented with blood stained pus discharge from the right ear with earache, vomiting and vertigo for 15 days. There was right sided lower motor neurone type of facial palsy for two days. Histopathology of the excised mass showed features of Rhabdomyosarcoma. Disease was extensive when the patient was first seen with involvement of middle ear, mastoid and brain but duration of symptoms was short. The propensity for the tumours to mimic otitis media at presentation may delay the diagnosis and management.
