N2  - The aim of this study was to find the incidence of facial nerve paralysis, evaluate the site of injury and the degree of paralysis and to measure the outcome of medical as well as surgical theraphy. Five hundred patients were screened for the presence of facial nerve paralysis. The incidence was found to be 9.6%. The site of injury and the degree of paralysis were evaluated by topognostic test,HRCT(high resolution CT)and NET (nerve excitability test). Management was decided upon after considering various assessment method, the most important, being the NET. NET values were evaluated during the followup period and they were compared. The results suggested that patients with NET difference >3.5mA required surgical exploration otherwise there were little chances of recovery with medical therapy. Thus the degree of paralysis on neuro diagnostic test has a definite role in diagnosis, management and its influience on recovery of facial nerve paralysis.
