N2  - We present a clinical case discussion of a 38 year old housewife who presented with a month history of mild fever, hepatomegaly, weight loss, dry cough, dyspnoea on exertion and raised serum alkaline phophatase level. The various clinical possibilities are discussed along with interpretation of subsequent investigations.
