N2  - The staged approach outlined here provides ophthalmic surgeons with a sound framework on which to base both clinical and surgical decisions in the management of patients with facial paralysis. Newer techniques, such as the SOOF lift, hard palate grafting, endoscopic brow lift, and botulinum A toxin injections provide more therapeutic options for such patients. These procedures help to correct not only the functional but the esthetic deficits caused by facial paralysis. This staged approach also provides patients with a set of reassuring goals.
