N2  - The authors discuss the problem of rehabilitation of a lesion of the upper branch of the facial nerve. They describe the technique-implantation of a golden weight into the upper lid-which they used in 12 patients. They emphasize the importance of oculoplastic surgery which eventually should become an integral part of contemporary treatment of facial nerve pareses.
