N2  - Granulomatous cheilitis is a skin disease of unknown etiology, either occuring isolated or accompanying Melkersson-Rosenthal-Syndrome. The disorder is preferably observed in middle-aged adults. A commonly accepted standard therapy is not known. In this case, we report about a male patient who suffered from granulomatous cheilitis since years, thereby revealing the disease as an early manifestation of Crohn's disease.
