N2  - There are many lips kinetic disorders whose clinical appearances greatly differ. An acute examination directs toward the diagnosis on a neurologic, neurogenous, muscular, myogenous, medicamentous, dermatological or psychiatric etiology. The authors review the different etiologies that have to be discussed, in order to choose the appropriate further investigations and specialized examinations, before a possible surgical treatment. © 2002 Éditions scientifiques et médicales Elsevier SAS. All rights reserved.
