N2  - A 13 years old male, a case of acute myeloid leukemia (AML-M2) in remission for six months developed facial nerve palsy with its involvement between geniculate ganglion and the corda tympani. CT scan revealed abnormal soft tissue in the left external auditory canal and middle ear cavity with destruction of the lateral wall of the facial nerve canal and involving the facial nerve. Minimal soft tissue mass was seen in the right middle ear suggesting an asymptomatic deposit. A biopsy from left external auditary canal confirmed the diagnosis of extramedullary myelogeneous deposit.
