N2  - Eosinophilic granuloma is one of the triad of conditions collectively known as Histiocytosis-X. It is an uncommon granulomatous disease which can affect the temporal bone. Although initially quiescent the disease may erode the mastoid cortex, destroy tegmen and extend into the cranial vault as well as erode the semicircular canals, cochlea or facial canal, giving rise to facial palsy. These lesions almost always become infected and can be confused with chronic otomastoiditis. When diagnosed, therapy consists of conservative surgery, radiation therapy, steroids and chemotherapy.
