N2  - The authors present two cases of Borreliosis characterized by a neurologic beginning. The first one showed myelitis symptoms, urine and bowels retention, spastic paraparesis and hypoesthesia with a D6-D7 level. The spinal RM images point-out hyperintense lesion in D6 at T2 sequence; the CSF showed an increase of cells and protein; the serologic ELISA test was positive for Borreliosis (confirmed by Western Blotting). The second one showed a polyneuritis with flaccid tetraparesis and left peripheral facial palsy. The ENG point-out a severe axonal polyneuropathy; the CSF showed albuminocytologic dissociation. Even in this case the serologic researches was positive for Borreliosis. The myelitis and the polyneuritis, more frequently, could be the first manifestation of Borreliosis. The Authors assert that a premature antibiotic treatment to reduces the chronicity of the disease chronication is necessary. They wish also a future epidemiologic italian panorama updating. In fact the trend has an increase of the disease in relation to a greater diagnostic accuracy.
