N2  - The authors developed an alternative technique for the treatment of eyebrow ptosis in facial palsy. The technique involves a subperiosteal pulling stitch that securely encircles the frontalis muscle at three points of the superior margin of the eyebrow. The stitch is directly fixed to the anterior aspect of the parietal cranium with an application of the threaded anchoring device. An effective and stable result of eyebrow elevation and a natural-looking appearance with some revived forehead wrinkles is provided by this internal suspension technique. This simplified and faster technique is strongly recommended to correct eyebrow ptosis; it has the advantages of a limited skin incision and no damage to the supraorbital and supratracheal nerves.
