N2  - We report here the case of a 67-year-old man who was treated successively with BICNU, mechlorthamine, radiotherapy, COP and interferon for a large plaque MF. Since six months he complained asthenia, sadness and felt depressed. Clinical examination revealed a cerebella syndrome, a pyramidal syndrome, facial paralyse. The diagnosis of cerebral lymphoma was confirmed. Psychiatric manifestations are not always related to interferon therapy and may be often the only expression of the cerebral localisation of the lymphoma.
