N2  - The secondary revision of a transferred flap is often needed for both functional and aesthetic reasons. In the past, this was accomplished by partial elevation of the flap with debulking and contouring, which requires a two-stage operation. Liposuction and lipoinjection, on the other hand, have become widely accepted techniques that allow aesthetic surgeons to sculpture fat in all body regions. It then is a natural extension that these techniques are used in flap revision. In this paper, the selection of cases where these techniques are indicated, devices that are useful for treatment and operative procedure are all discussed, and some results are demonstrated. As a result, liposuction could markedly improve the aesthetic appearance with appropriate planning and technique. Moreover, liposuction could also be indicated for cases of facial paralysis needing some revision after a latissimus dorsi muscle flap transfer. Lipoinjection was indicated for those cases that have a small hollow with a good wound bed. However, the effectiveness was uncertain, because of the short follow-up time.
