N2  - A case of Wegener's granulomatosis, which presented as chronic otitis media with facial nerve palsy, is described. Early diagnosis is vital if unnecessary surgical exploration is to be avoided. A false negative cANCA may delay the diagnosis, especially in cases of locoregional disease, and a policy of repeated titres should be adopted, if clinical suspicion is high.
