N2  - This article focuses on the risks related to intentional or inadvertent use of prostaglandins analogs (in particular misoprostol) and NSAIDs during pregnancy. The potentially important rote of cyclooxygenase-2 in obstetrics and in foetus development is emphasised. Prescription of combined NSAIDs-misoprostol preparations is strongly contraindicated during pregnancy and selective cyclooxygenase-2 inhibitors should as welt be avoided due to currently available data suggesting a possible perturbation of several obstetrical processes and of foetal kidney development.
