N2  - Wegener's Granulomatosis is a granulomatous necrotizing vasculitis described by Frederich Wegener as recently as 1936, usually affecting both high and low airway and renal glomerule and rarely small vessels in any other location. Facial nerve palsy has been reported during the curse of the disease, but only in few cases it was the initial manifestation of the condition. We present a patient with chronic otitis media and facial palsy in which Wegener Granulomatosis was diagnosed in spite of the scarcity of any other symptoms. The case is discussed and the literature is reviewed.
