N2  - Heerfoldet syndrome is an unusual manifestation of systemic sarcoidosis and is characterized by parotitis, uveitis, and facial nerve paralysis. A 77-year-old female with a diagnosis of malignant lymphoma was referred to us for left facial nerve paralysis and left otalgia. After we treated her with intravenous administration of steroids and acyclovir as Rumsey Hunt Syndrome, the facial nerve paralysis was revealed to be caused by sarcoidosis. Because this case had only two of three characteristic symptoms of Heerfoldt syndrome, facial nerve paralysis and uveitis, we made the diagnosis of incomplete type of Heerfoldt syndrome.
