N2  - Tumors in the parotid region often involve facial nerve branches and wide resection usually results in severe depression deformity and, therefore, facial paralysis. The free flap offers a good reconstructive option, achieving good contour as well as facial animation. In primary reconstruction, a free rectus abdominis musculocutaneous flap with a sural nerve graft is a good procedure. In secondary reconstruction, micro-neurovascular free muscle transfer seems necessary when the mimetic muscles develop irreversible atrophy. Restoration of facial nerve function as well as facial contour would be the key points to achieving a good quality of life for the patients who undergo wide resection of cheek-tumors.
