N2  - This article looks at the 6 'ventus' foramina ('wind points', whose names include the Chinese character feng 'ventus' ('wind'): aula venti, Rg16 ('Assembly hall of the wind', fengfu); stagnum venti, F20 ('Pool of the wind', fengchi); porta ventorum, V12 ('Gate of winds', fengmen); forum ventorum, F31 ('Market place of the winds', feng-shi); pluteus venti, T17 ('Protective screen against the wind', yifeng); continens ventum, IT12 ('Provides for control of the ventus', bing-feng). At first, it gives classical text references which provide a more exact explanation of these names, then it goes into the details of the physiological particularities of 'ventus' foramina ('wind points'): All the foramina are on the yang conduits and are mostly foramina copulo-conventoria ('Points of connection and meeting', jiaohui xue). They are all located on the yang parts of the body, in places where the muscle and the skin are relatively thin and soft, and where their deepest layers reach into important anatomical areas. On the one hand, these are places which are easily accessible to ventus ('wind') heteropathies and, on the other hand, they are important foramina for the expulsion of ventus. This is why, for all illnesses connected with ventus (ventus internus ['internal wind'] and also ventus externus ['external wind']) these 'ventus' foramina can be used as the main foramina or in combination. Above all, in cases of pathological disturbances resulting from ventus externus ('external wind') some of these foramina are indicated, namely, porta ventorum, V12 ('Gate of winds', fengmen), forum ventorum, F31 ('Market place of the winds', fengshi); pluteus venti, T17 ('Protective screen against the wind', yifeng) and continens ventum, IT12 ('Provides for control of the ventus', bingfeng), whereas foramina such as aula venti, Rg16 ('Assembly hall of the wind', fengfu); stagnum venti, F20 ('Pool of wind', fengchi) can be used in the treatment of both ventus externus and ventus internus ('external and internal wind'). In an attempt to specifically dispel ventus and remove occlusiones (bi-syndromes), the appropriate 'ventus' foramina for clinical practice are named in combination with other suitable foramina for the therapy of externally-induced extima ('surface') symptoms, itching, occlusio (bi) pains in the joints, distortion of the eyes and mouth as a result of hemiplegia (facial pareses), dizziness and headaches as well as symptoms induced by vento percussio ('being affected by ventus', apoplexy, zhongfeng) with signs of paralysis.
