N2  - In this retrospective study, patients with Bell's palsy who received Prednisolone and Acyclovir combination treatment were compared with those who received Prednisolone only in a tertiary ENT hospital. There were 21 patients with Bell's palsy during the study period of 30 months. There were 11 patients in the Prednisolone and Acyclovir combination group, 8 in the Prednisolone only group, and 2 patients did not receive any medication. In the Prednisolone and Acyclovir group, 4 patients showed significant clinical improvement at 2 weeks (p = 0.042) and 8 patients showed improvement at 4 weeks (p = 0.005), whereas none of the patients in the Prednisolone group showed significant clinical improvement at 2 weeks, and only 1 patient had improvement at 4 weeks. Though the numbers were small, the results show a clear trend towards early recovery in patients who received combination treatment with prednisolone and acyclovir.
