N2  - We present a case of a 54-year old man with Ramsay-Hunt syndrome. The characteristic constellation of facial nerve paralysis in association with herpetic eruption (in our patient in dermatorne C2) and complications of vestibulo-cochlear dysfunction was present. The trigeminal nerve and cervical dermatome C2 were also involved. MRI showed an abnormal enhancement of the facial nerve involving the geniculate ganglion. After systemic acyclovir therapy most symptoms recovered with the exception of hearing loss.
