N2  - Objectives: To evaluate the effects of a combination therapy of amphotericin B plus itraconazole versus monotherapy with amphotericin B or itraconazole in the rhino-orbital mucormycosis. Patients and methods: We report two cases of rhino-orbital mucormycosis. Two women 56 and 70 years old, both suffering from decompensated diabetes mellitus, had shown an abrupt onset of the disease with pain on the right face and homolateral involvement of the right orbit. On admission they showed an exophthalmus with a total ophthalmoplegia of the right eye and peripheral paralysis of the right facial nerve. Results: In the first case, after a cycle with amphotericin B not resolutive, we got recovery after a second therapeutic cycle with itraconazole. In the second case we achieved a faster resolution of the infection with a combination therapy with amphotericin B plus itraconazole. Conclusions: In the rhino-orbital mucormycosis a combination therapy with amphotericin B plus itraconazole showed to be more effective than a monotherapy with amphotericin B or itraconazole.
