N2  - OBJECTIVE: To investigate operative effect on serious advanced facial paralysis. METHOD: 28 cases (28 sides) with serious facial paralysis underwent decompression or transplantation of facial nerve. RESULT: After following up 0.5-2 years postoperatively, the total, most or partial and no recovery were 14 cases (50%), 12 cases (42%) and 2 cases (7.1%) respectively. CONCLUSION: The operation performed as early as possible can be an effective procedure for correcting serious advanced facial paralysis if conservative treatment could be confirmed to be helpless.
