N2  - Ramsay Hunt syndrome consists of facial palsy, audiological loss and herpetic lesions at the auricle. It is caused by the reactivation of the varicella-zoster virus. This syndrome has been associated with several risk factors, some of them highly prevalent in the general population, and it often presents audiological or neurological complications. It is worth remembering some clinical, epidemiological and therapeutic aspects of the Ramsay Hunt syndrome, as its diagnosis and treatment could be assumed by the Family Physician in the absence of complications.
