N2  - Malignant otitis externa is an uncommon, but serious condition occurring usually in elderly diabetic or immunosuppressed patients. Hairy Cell Leukaemia is a rare, B cell lymphoproliferative disorder which causes pancytopaenia with morbidity and mortality most commonly due to opportunistic infection. A case of malignant otitis externa where Hairy Cell Leukaemia may be a predisposing factor is presented.
