N2  - This study report a case of a patient with severe Miller-Fisher syndrome (tetraparetic and cranial nerves disturbances), that was treated with intravenous immunoglobulin (IVIg) at the dose of 0.35 g/kg/day. There was neurologic improvement, followed by clinical deterioration one week later. A second course of IVIg was given with definitive improvement. The authors review the literature. Conclusions are that IVIg has similar results than plasma exchange and that is important a closely observation during the first weeks after IVIg treatment.
