N2  - In patients with bulbar paralysis, amyotrophic lateral sclerosis, M. Parkinson, infantile brain damage, and complete facial denervation, severe sialorrhoea and drooling, where oral medical treatment fails, botulinum toxin A injection of the parotid glands cah provide an alternative. Preliminary results of eight patients are reported. Patients with complete facial denervation need contralateral injections because of the atrophy of the homolateral parotid gland.
