N2  - Acoustic neuroma is a relatively rare complaint. The ocular complications arise in cases of injury to a facial nerve or to the intermediary Wrisberg nerve. The result is problems of ocular dryness and corneal complications with damage to the epithelium and endothelium. In cases of both permanent and temporary facial paralysis, the permanent wearing of soft lenses is a very poor indication. In these cases, a permanent hard lens with a high Dk level should be used as a therapeutic lens. Even in the absence of facial paralysis, in a significant number of cases where there has been injury to the intermediary Wrisberg nerve, a dry eye and corneal fragility demande great caution on the part of the patient may be observed.
