N2  - The ability of acoustic analysis to detect slight acoustic differences confirms the usefulness of this method in evaluating the extent of impairment, as well as its value in prognosis. Speech therapy should reinforce the slight contrast detected by the spectrum analysis. The case of a pseudobulbar palsy patient merits description and attention for two main reasons: the paralysis is limited to the lingual function and recovery is complete. Such pseudo-opercular syndromes without any other motor deficits have better prognosis than usual pontine infarcts.
