N2  - A review of 38 patients operated for meningioma of the pontocerebellar angle on Neurosurgical Division of Varese Regional Hospital is carried out to elucidate the problems of this surgical approach. Meningiomas were divided into little (4 patients), medium (14 patients) and large (20 patients). Neurological symptoms and signs were related to wideness and to dural origin of the neoplasm. In all patients surgical approach was the suboccipital retromastoid route performed in sitting position with head moderately flexed. Surgical extirpation was demonstrated to be Simpson grade 1-2 in 30 patients and to be Simpson 3-4 in 8 patients. Three patients dead postoperatively. In the follow up 76.3% of patients had a good result. The surgical approach, the relationship between surgical extirpation and tumoral firmness and the pre- postoperative deficits of facial nerve are debated.
