N2  - Purpose: To present a case of a woman diagnosed of uterine leiomyosarcoma with middle ear metastasis. Material and methods: A 56-year- old woman with initial presentation of chronic serous otitis media who developed a peripheral facial paralysis. After a careful study, the origin of the otitis was found as secondary to a middle ear metastasis from a uterine leiomyosarcoma. Results: The case is described standing out the peculiar natural history with an aggressive evolution, and the brilliant response to the administered chemotherapy protocol. Conclusions: The authors make a review of the medical literature and the etiologic characteristics of the temporal bone space occupant lesions, confirming the exceptionally of a middle ear metastasis due to uterine leiomyosarcoma.
