N2  - Traumatic head injuries are the principal cause of death and physical disability in young people. Sometimes a base of the skull fracture is produced, wounding the temporal bone structures in the 50% of patients. So that, can be observed some clinical findings and complications for each type of fracture e, wich must be treated, surgically or conservatively, by the otorhinolaryngologist in cooperation with neurosurgeons and other specialists. The clinical diagnosis will be confirmed with computerized tomography. The consequences of the temporal bone fractures includes: hearing loss, vestibular dysfunction and facial nerve injury.
