N2  - A 70-year-old women presented with dizziness, hearing impairment in the left side and left facial palsy. MRI-Gd revealed a homogeneously enhanced mass of 1 cm in size in the left internal acoustic meatus. But the mass was growing up to 3 cm and invaded to the leptomenix for three months. Mental status was decling. Diagnosis of B-cell lymphoma was made on the basis of positive CSF cytology. We performed chemotherapy but the patient died.
