N2  - 186 patients suffering from peripheral facial paralysis were treated principally with acupuncture, at the same time Chinese herbal drugs were given orally in some severe cases. According to the basic theories of traditional Chinese medicine peripheral. Facial paralysis is divided into three types, namely, the deficiency of both qi and blood with exopathic wind, the deficiency of liver-yin and kidney-yin with exopathic wind, and blood- heart type. Each of the types was treated principally with acupuncture, at the same time vitamin B1 and B12 were given intramuscularly: and in addition to it herbal decoctum was given orally in severe cases. Results showed that 169 cases (90.86%) recovered completely, and the therapy seemed to be effective in 13 cases (6.98%), while 4 cases (2.15%) just showed improvement in the condition. The total effective rate of the theory, is 100%.
