N2  - The implantation of gold weights into the upper eyelid ('lid-loading') has been proved to be effective in the therapy of facial palsy. On 14 patients with unilateral facial palsy skin-toned tantalum weights, that were fixed external to the upper eyelid, were used for the treatment of lagophthalmus ('external lid-loading'). An existing exposure keratitis could be improved in all cases, respectively the development was avoided from the beginning. The major problem for the patients was the difficult handling of the adhesive strips as well as the fixation of the weights in case of existing dermatochalasis. This new technique is suitable for reversible facial palsies (Bell's palsies), also in addition to the local therapy with drops and ointments. The difficult application of the adhesive strips is in need of improvement, this led to an earlier ending of the therapy especially of older patients.
