N2  - We report a case of a 28 years old woman who, in August 1993, presented with right facial palsy, deficit of the right 6th cranial nerve, sensitive loss in the territory of the right first trigeminal branch and in the right arm, mild aphasia nominum, signs of cerebellar involvement. Cranial MRI was performed, and we suspected a possible demyelinative disease; this hypothesis was not confirmed by VEP and cerebrospinal fluid analysis. Then, we looked for antiborrelia antibodies, which resulted positive in two consecutive samples. The patient was treated with Doxacicline (100 mg X2/die), and fast clinical recovery was obtained: we therefore diagnosed Neuroborreliosis with Central Nervous System involvement.
