N2  - Based on favorable experiences with acupuncture for the treatment of facial palsy in humans, a clinical trial using electroacupuncture was carried out over a 3-year period involving 12 horses with unilateral facial paralysis of traumatic origin. The inclusion of a control group was not possible because all owners sought treatment with acupuncture for their horses. Treatments were administered every other day by applying 150 to 300mV at 125Hz to eight acupuncture points per treatment. The number of treatments required to achieve full recovery in all horses was approximately 13. No statistically significant correlation between the severity of the facial paralysis and the number of treatments needed for full recovery was found. No adverse effects were observed. Use of this technique is proposed for large- scale clinical trials.
