N2  - Melkersson-Rosenthal syndrome is characterized by facial paralysis, facial edema and lingua plicata. We show three cases: two incompleted cases and a complete one. There aren't neither allergic base, nor family character, nor associating infections. A just case had relation with autoimmune disease. All of them are factors which are relationed with this syndrome. Our cases subsided with glucocorticosteroids, without other alternative therapy (sulfanilamides, metronidazole or clofazimine).
