N2  - Most of the facial paralysis are Bell's palsy, but before to select this diagnosis, particularly in emergency, the physician must research other etiologies as viral infection (herpes zoster), meningitis... In case of trauma, the initial grading of the paralysis, the associated lesions and C.T. Scan results, will determinate the opportunity of surgical treatment. In all cases, a particular care will be done for eye protection. If the recovery of the facial function, after weeks, is non-existent, the diagnosis of Bell's palsy will be discuss, and another etiology suspected, like a tumor of the facial nerve.
