N2  - A 42 year old woman was complaining of left facial palsy even after kinds of treatment had been performed in other hospitals. Radiological examinations revealed an irregular mass shadow with bony destruction in the left temporal bone. The mass was histologically diagnosed as chondrosar coma. It was removed by skull base surgery with transmastoid approach. Clinical manifestations and treatment methods of the temporal bone chondrosarcoma were discussed.
