N2  - Salivary duct carcinoma is rare and was first described by Kleinsasser in 1968. We present a 59-year old female who complained of right facial paresis associated with parotid gland carcinoma. Total parotidectomy including right facial nerve transection and right supraomohyoid neck dissection was performed. Despite of this operative procedures and postoperative radiotherapy, the patient died of distant metastasis.
