N2  - Seven patients with head and neck sarcoidosis were treated from 1971 to 1995. There were one male and six females aged from 27 to 52 years. They manifested various clinical symptoms, such as neck mass in seven cases, proxymal facial palsy in two cases, and oral epipharynx lymphoid mass in two cases. Pathologic samples were obtained from the neck mass in five cases and from the epipharyngeal mass in two cases. Three cases, who manifested symptoms only in the otolaryngologic region, showed spontaneous remission without any treatment.
