N2  - Aesthetic facial rejuvenation has become more acceptable and commonplace, most likely fueled by the baby boom generation beginning to suffer the ravages of time. As more and younger patients seek facial rejuvenation, surgeons have been seeking enhanced approaches, improved in the sense of yielding results that are the same or better while at the same time decreasing the perioperative and postoperative sequelae. The endoscope was adapted to forehead and facelift surgery with these objectives in mind. The design of this review is to provide my opinion on how the endoscope can be useful for rejuvenation of the midface and the subperiosteal brow lift. The endoscopic malar pad lift is a technique developed by me to selectively lift the midface. This approach can also be used in conjunction with a subperiosteal brow lift, a facelift, or both.
