N2  - A child aged 7 years with multiple sclerosis developed diplopia, vertigo, facial palsy, bearing loss visual disorder within 3 months. Neurotological examination revealed brain stem disorder. Multiple high signal lesions appeared within the periventricular white matter on T2 weighted MRI. After treatment with prednisolone, she showed gradually improvement. About a year later she became completely free from symptoms.
