N2  - This study highlights paralysis of the orbicularis oculi as the main sequel of facial palsy and its following progressive course. A varied etiology emphasizes the need for a complete ophthalmological, E.N.T., medical and neurologic checkup in every case of facial palsy. This knowledge allows the therapy to be tailored to each individual case. The management of facial palsy is primarily based on the patient's facial motor function, lacrimal secretion and corneal sensation.
