N2  - Herpes tester (HZ) is the reactivation in adults of varicella-zoster virus (VZV) infection. At least 95% of the U.S. population is latently infected by VZV. The most common cause of morbidity associated with HZ is pain, which may present as prodromal pain, acute pain, or postherpetic neuralgia (PHN) and which may be very difficult to manage to the patient's satisfaction. The duration and severity of pain appear most severe in elderly patients. While the mainstay of treatment of HZ has been acyclovir, its newly approved prodrug valacyclovir offers several advantages that result from improved bioavailability. Famciclovir, a prodrug of penciclovir, appears to have efficacy equivalent to acyclovir in most parameters of healing, although there are few published studies regarding its use.
