N2  - The author, having done a detailed review of the anatomy and physiology of the facial nerve, describes the Facial Peripheric Palsy in its ethiologic, clinical and diagnostic aspects; taking special care with 'Frigore Palsy' the most ordinary cause of the illness. The different options in the Physiatric treatment are related with it's physiologic bases. Finally, the author emphasizes the role of the Rehabilitation Medicine.
