N2  - A 50-year-old woman with uveitis, fever, right peripheral facial palsy and swelling of bilateral parotid glands as initial manifestations was diagnosed as having Heerfordt's syndrome in 1989. She had palsies of other cranial nerves. After the administration of corticosteroids for about 4 years, alkaliphosphatase (ALP) began to increase gradually. There were multiple low density areas throughout the liver in the abdominal CT. The needle biopsy revealed epitheloid granulomas in the liver. The administration of 60 mg of prednisolone every other day, resulted in disappearance of the low density areas in the liver confirmed by CT and decrease in serum ACE and ALP levels. The hepatic sarcoidosis with liver dysfunction is uncommon in Japan.
