N2  - The effect of physiotherapy on patients after 12 months had elapsed following facial nerve paralysis was analysed using objective and subjective measurements. The analysis of objective scores of synkinesis, tone, and movement grading, as well as self report measures, supports the benefits of physiotherapy for these patients. The House-Brackmann grades, however, do not reflect these findings. A more refined objective measurement tool is required to assess facial nerve paralysis.
