N2  - Different techniques can be used to repair paralytic labial commissurae. Ideally, microsurgical procedures or dynamic suspension methods can correct kinetic paralysis but in certain patients (elderly subjects, poor general health, precarious postsurgical rehabilitation) such procedures may represent an excessively aggressive procedure. We therefore used static suspension of the paralytic labial commissurae based on desepidermization of a nasogeneal flap. This simple technique is easy to perform and is our method of choice for static suspension because the flap pulls the paralysed commissurae upward and doubles the tissue cover, helping overcome buccinator incompetence.
