N2  - A case of herpes zoster oticus with facial paralysis, sensorineural deafness and disequilibrium has been studied with pre- and post-contrast MRI of the petrous bone. Enhancement was observed in the entire area of the labyrinthine segment of the internal auditory canal. Not only the facial nerve but also the vestibular and cochlear nerve were involved. Thus, we have found MRI to be a unique method to localize the site and the dimension of nerve injury in herpes zoster oticus.
