N2  - In most cases of idiopathic facial paralysis we have found an elevated antiviral antibodies titre and an alteration of the immunitary lymphocyte-mediated system expressed by the abnormal values of the OKT4/OKT8 relation and of the OKT3 index (total lymphocytes). Therefore Bell's palsy pathogenesis can be directly or indirectly related to a viral infection as proved in the work effected in 1977 in the ORL Division of the L'Aquila Civil Hospital entitled: 'Aspects immunofluoroscopiques de la corde du tympan sur des sujets atteints de paralysie de Bell' (Giannoni-Corbacelli). In a group of 125 patients with Bell's paralysis we have proposed different pharmacological treatments evidencing shorter hospital stay and a shorter recovery in the group treated with Tp5.
