N2  - Facial nerve palsy is a well recognised complication of Acute Otitis Media in children. Four cases are reported here. All were boys between 1 and 2 1/2 years of age, 3 presenting with complete facial paralysis. All were treated with myringotomy, grommet insertion and antibiotics, and all made a complete recovery. Review of the literature shows that there is still disagreement about the optimal management of this disorder, but most authors would advocate initial treatment with myringotomy, grommet insertion and antibiotics in the absence of other pathology.
