N2  - A double-blind study evaluated naftidrofuryl in 21 cases of Bell's palsy with complete axonal degeneration and no response of the nerve to stimulation at inclusion in the trial, which occurred seven days after onset. Corticosteroid therapy was given to all patients. A clinical and electrophysiological evaluation was performed on days seven, 37, and 97. The naftidrofuryl group showed faster functional recovery with a return to normal of facial nerve motor latencies. Evoked motor response amplitudes for the four muscles evaluated (orbicularis oris, orbicularis oculi, mentalis muscle and corrugator supercilii) were significantly higher in naftidrofuryl group than in the control group. These data suggest that naftidrofuryl may be beneficial for the treatment of a frigore facial palsy.
