N2  - The authors studied 12 cases of malignant exterial otitis between 1982 and 1992, at ENT Department of Hospital das Clinicas da Universidade de Sao Paulo. The disease was most prevalent in the male sex and between ages 21-30 and older than 60. Diabetes was present in 50% of the patients. Otorrhea was the main complaint (100%), followed by pain (58%). Most of the patients had some kind of neurosensorial hearing loss (75%). Facial palsy occurred, as a complication, in 58%. All patients were submitted to drug treatment and only one had to go to the operating room. The aim of this paper is to discuss the diagnostic, treatment and prognostic problems.
