N2  - Hemifacial spasm (idiopathic in 9 cases or following a facial nerve palsy in 9 cases) can represent a real handicap for the patient. The treatment, consisting of repeated botulinus toxin injections, is only proposed when a compression of the nerve (BERA, IRM, EMG, surgical exploration in young patients) has been excluded and when medical treatment has proved unsuccessful. 18 patients were treated with these injections. Subjective results are considered satisfactory in 100% of cases. Objective results are good in 60% of cases and moderate in 40%. Two transient complications were observed: one facial palsy and one case of dry eye.
