N2  - Since 1986, we have treated thirty seven Ramsay-Hunt syndromes, out of two hundred and eight peripheral acute facial palsies. Twenty patients were seen before the third week of evolution, ten of whom benefitted from a treatment with Acyclovir administered intravenously for seven days at the dose of 30 mg/kg-1 day-1. Seventeen were examined late, after three weeks. The compared functional prognosis of the different subgroups shows significant differences: patients treated with Acyclovir early all recovered a normal facial function within six months. For the others, the functional prognosis even after surgical treatment was mediocre, in agreement with the reputation of severity of virus zoster varicella (VZV) impairment.
