N2  - A physiotherapy programme designed to maximise recovery following facial paralysis is presented. Treatment includes thermal stimulation and soft tissue massage at the stage of complete lower motor neurone paralysis, and specific facial muscle exercises when movement recommences. Motor Sensory Re-Education (M.S.R.E.) or biofeedback is employed to increase facial muscle activity, or to decrease other activity in the case of synkinesis.
