N2  - A 23 year old female with an 18 month history of right sided facial palsy following surgery for a fourth ventricle venous angioma was successfully treated with a cross facial nerve graft. The functional and aesthetic advantages of reinervating the facial musculature in this young patient. despite the long duration of palsy, warranted an attempt at treatment using the cross facial graft. Hyperkinesis on the nonparalysed side in the form of a facial tic further facilitated this method of reanimation. This paper demonstrates that cross facial nerve grafting continues to have an application in the management of facial palsy.
