N2  - Idiopathic facial paralysis is a therapeutic emergency, since functional and esthetic sequelae depend upon the management and rapidity of treatment. Following an anatomical and physiological review, the authors, based on their experience of 900 cases a year, describe the essential early clinical evaluation with its precise scoring of muscle groups, electrical tests and measurement of two reflexes of prognostic value, discuss the indication of NMR and detail therapeutic choice factors on the basis of this evaluation, stressing the large number of special cases. Monitoring of the patient and the outcome are described.
