N2  - Two patients with severe cerebellar ataxia of gait associated with the Ramsay Hunt syndrome of herpes zoster are reported, and the literature of zoster-related ataxia is reviewed. Clinicopathological correlation is unclear since patients with ataxia have not been shown to have cerebellar lesions, and the few cases with cerebellar pathology have not had cerebellar syndromes. Herpes zoster, particularly cephalic herpes, may have serious neurological sequelae. We thus outline a treatment protocol for herpes zoster.
