N2  - Otologic and neurotologic manifestations associated with HIV infection and AIDS occur but are less prevalent than other head and neck complaints. In the majority of cases, otologic disease is caused by routine organisms and responds to standard therapy. Often the ear disease is not directly related to the HIV infection. KS of the ear, P. carinii otitis, eustachian tube obstruction owing to nasopharyngeal mass, SOM, ABR abnormalities, sensorineural hearing loss secondary to central nervous system complications of AIDS, and facial nerve palsy constitute true otologic manifestations associated with HIV infection.
