N2  - The use of type A botulinum toxin for the treatment of blepharospasm and facial spasm in widespread in our medium. For this reason, we proposed to carry out intensive monitoring of adverse reactions to this treatment, studying both those that are produced at the time of injection and those that appear within a six-month period. The pharmacist present at the time of injection collects the pertinent data and explains to the patient how to fill out a self-evaluation survey at home. The monitoring ends with a final interview when the survey is collected. Severe adverse reactions are not observed; most are local and transitory, and include ecchymosis and blepharoptosis. The treatment is not associated with important risks to the patient.
