N2  - Facial palsy is a relatively uncommon condition with a variety of causes including dental intervention. A brief history of two cases of facial palsy with dental implications is presented. The aetiology of facial palsy is reviewed and the management of such cases is discussed. The option of immediate treatment of Bell's palsy with prednisone is stressed.
