N2  - Between the causes of facial paralysis, similar to Bell's palsy, recently are included those due to some family's of spirochaete (Borrelia burgdorferi) transmitted through tick-bite. These bacteria, besides the facial palsy, may produce several degrees of lymphocytic meningitis and subsequently the paralysis of the face, sometimes clumsy or recurrent. The treatment being the antibiotic drugs, never the corticoids. In the paper are explained prospectively the incidence of this disease in the AA's environment.
