N2  - The classical triad of signs in Melkersson Rosenthal's syndrome(MRS) consists of recurrent swelling of the lips and face, facial paresis,and scrotal tongue; these features are frequently accompanied by minor symptoms, including migrainous headaches. We report on a 62-years-old female patient, who had been suffering from typical, recurrent Melkersson-Rosenthal's syndrome for 39 years. 3 years ago, she developed concomitant arteriitis temporalis. We discuss the possible interrelation of these diseases.
