N2  - Lyme disease was recognized initially as epidemic oligoarthritis. Intensive investigation has resulted in the clarification of the cause, epidemiology, natural history, and successful treatment of Lyme disease. Although Lyme disease is a public health problem only in certain geographic areas, it has now been reported in 39 states is the the most common tick-related illness in the continental United States. Lyme disease must remain a clinical diagnosis, because the serologic tests that are now generally available are accurate but inherently variable, and they pose particular problems in diagnosing Lyme disease in endemic areas. Specialized assays currently in development should prove useful in the future.
