N2  - A brief historical introduction of facial paralysis is given. Recent trends in treatment of palsy of the VIIth cranial nerve are analysed. Only the dynamic approach is considered. The classical methods of suspension by fascia lata, neurotomy and selective controlateral myotomy are not discussed. Lesions are divided into: - extra-cranial or recent intratemporal, - recent intracranial, - inveterate, according to physiology and morphological and functional dynamics. Surgical procedures are proposed (as most suitable) for the various clinical conditions. These are neuroraphy and nerve graft for extracranial or intratemporal lesions, nerve graft with contralateral anastomosis (cross face) for recent intracranial lesions and nerve graft with contralateral anastomosis and vascularized muscle graft for inveterate lesions. Results of prospects are discussed.
