N2  - The effect of flunarizine, a calcium antagonist, on experimentally induced facial nerve injury in guinea pigs was studied electron microscopically. In flunarizine-untreated animals, intra-axonal accumulation of cell organelles and degradation of myelin sheaths were observed. In flunarizine-treated animals, these changes were not observed, but a knob-like protrusion of myelin sheaths and a structure resembling the myelin sheath in Schwann cell cytoplasm was occasionally observerd.
