N2  - Tumors of the intraparotid facial nerve are rare. They may simulate the more common parotid gland tumors. A correct pre-operative diagnosis is exceptional. They are usually benign, and their treatment is surgical excision, with repair of the facial nerve under microscope if necessary. The authors report one case of neurofibroma of the facial nerve trunk treated by resection and immediate repair by nerve grafting, with good rehabilitation of facial movement.
