N2  - Adverse hepatic reactions to nitrofurantoin therapy are well reported and range from acute cholestatic or hepatitic injury to chronic active hepatitis. Neurological side-effects, predominantly sensorimotor peripheral polyneuropathy, have also been documented. We report the first case of combined neurological and hepatic reaction to nitrofurantoin; this occurred during repeated treatment with the drug.
