N2  - An extremely rare case of traumatic thermal injury of the middle and inner ear with deafness and irreversible peripheral facial palsy is presented. The accident was caused by a metal spark perforating the tympanic membrane during welding. The risk of ear damage during welding is not generally appreciated and the welding masks normally used offer no protection to the ears. This serious case, as well as other reported injuries, emphasizes the fact that welders ought to protect not only the eyes but also the ears.
