N2  - Tuberculosis of the middle ear was found in 2.6% of the operated cases of chronic suppurative otitis media (CSOM). Primary tuberculosis of the middle ear was seen in 3 cases, and secondary tuberculosis in 4 cases. The youngest case was of a 3 year female child and eldest of a 14 year female. Periauricular fistula was encountered in 5 cases; facial nerve paralysis of lower motor neurone type in 2 cases of which 1 had meningitis; and infra-auricular lymphadenopathy was seen in 3 cases. Moderate hearing loss was present in 5 cases and severe hearing loss in 2 cases. Diagnosis was confirmed by histopathological examination. All the cases were treated by combination of anti-tubercular drugs and surgery in the form of mastoid exploration.
