N2  - In 132 previously untreated cases of peripheral facial palsy the serological tests in CF antibody and HI antibody titers was performed. They were positive in 55.5% of Bell's palsy, in contrast 86.4% (p < 0.05) of Hunt syndrome. Infected viruses were mainly herpes simplex, herpes zoster and cytomegalovirus. Prognosis was significantly poor in Hunt syndrome with negative antibodies. The patients had a good result in the cases of combined infection, but significantly poor in Hunt syndrome with steroid therapy.
