N2  - Eight patients with severe peripheral facial paralysis were treated with continuous epidural blocks. Cannulas were introduced between the seventh cervical and the fourth thoracic spinous process. Six ml of 0.25% bupivacaine or 1% liducaine were injected through the cannulas, 2 to 5 times a day, for about a month. Their conditions were evaluated with paralysis scores. They showed almost complete recoveries within three months after onset and had no major complication.
