N2  - Bilateral facial nerve palsy is a rare disease. In the past 30 years only 11 cases of bilateral simultaneous Bell's palsy have been reported, and only three were completely simultaneous. This is a case report of complete simultaneous Bell's palsy. The patient was a 27-year-old man. On March 18, 1984, he noted facial nerve palsy that occurred simultaneously on both sides. He visited us with a complaint of difficulty in talking on April 24, 1984. Bell's palsy was diagnosed, because physical findings and laboratory examinations showed no evidence of systemic diseases. About 6 months after onset, his palsy had subsided almost completely bilaterally following conservative treatment.
