N2  - A case of facial palsy due to malignant myeloma of the temporal bone is presented. Although malignancy in the temporal bone is a well-recognized cause of facial palsy, myeloma has not previously been specifically recorded as such a cause. The case described is interesting in that the tumour was visible on otoscopy and appropriate treatment resulted in considerable improvement in the facial weakness.
