N2  - A case of von Recklinghausen's disease has been observed for 6 years. The patient was a 22-year-old male. He visited the otolaryngology clinic with complaints of bilateral hearing loss, right facial palsy, right ophthalmoplegia, gait disturbance, and bilateral muscle atrophy of the extremities. Swelling was noted in the right neck and pharyngo-laryngeal area. Cafe au lait spots were noticed. The bilateral hearing loss was caused by bilateral acoustic neurinomas, which were confirmed by CT-scan examination. The hearing loss gradually progressed. The patient was young and had tumors in many cranial nerves, therefore the treatment should have been performed very carefully.
