N2  - This paper deals with the fact that the suppressive effect of the percutaneous needle prick on the facial nerve can be added up by repeating the traumatic insults. It was concluded that if properly repeated, needle prick trauma on facial nerve can cure the hemifacial spasm for about six months without producing facial palsy.
