N2  - Fifty-three patients were examined after head trauma followed by otological complications. In 79% of cases the patients were aged from 11 to 40 years. In 36% of cases the cause of trauma was traffic accident. The most serious traumas included fractures of the cranial base involving the pyramid - they accounted for 26% of radiologically confirmed skull fractures. Hearing impairment was found in 77% of cases, and 27% of them had complete deafness. In 57% of cases facial nerve damage was present and in 33% of cases permanent paralysis of this nerve remained. In 38% of cases surgical intervention was required for otological reasons and in 24% of cases this intervention was necessary because of facial nerve injury.
