N2  - The clinical manifestations of cytomegalovirus (CMV) infection are diverse. In common with other herpes viruses, it has been a predilection for involvement of the nervous system and it can cause aseptic meningitis, encephalitis and Guillain-Barre type polyneuritis. A case is described here of primary generalized CMV infection presenting with an isolated Bell's palsy in a pregnant woman. The potential hazards of corticosteroid therapy for Bell's palsy in pregnancy are stressed.
