N2  - The palliative treatment of longstanding facial paralysis aims at compensating for the global deficit of all the motor musculature of the hemi-face. Cutaneous plastic surgery comprises two stages: the upper stage and the lower stage. For the upper stage, the authors regard surgery of the frontal eyebrow ptosis as treatment of the paralysis of the orbital muscles of the eyelid. For the lower stage there is the face lift and Pitanguy flap, a nasogenic excision which consists of epidermizing a genian elliptical flap and rotating the superior branch, which is attached to the malleary periosteum, while the inferior branch is sutured to the buccal commissure. The resulting over-correction reduces in time. On the whole, the authors have described simple methods giving immediate, esthetically acceptable results.
