N2  - The surgical reconstruction of an established facial paralysis is one of the most demanding tasks of the reconstructive surgeon. The 16 mimic muscles on each side of the face are controlled by the facial nerve. They function independently and in concert to provide three different functions. These functions are the production of facial tone, voluntary facial movement, and involuntary facial expression. The technique of muscle transplantation can be applied to any one of the muscles that are available for transplantation by microneurovascular techniques. There are three stages to any muscle transplantation. The first two, preparation of the muscle for transplantation and preparation of the recipient site, which precede muscle transplantation, may frequently be done simultaneously by two teams, thus shortening the overall length of the procedure.
