N2  - Four cases of bilateral simultaneous facial palsy had different causes such as Ramsay-Hunt syndrome, Bell's palsy, acute promyelocytic leukemia and metastatic cerebello-pontine angle tumor. From these four cases the following points were concluded: In Ramsay-Hunt syndrome, palsy on the firstly involved side was severer than that of the secondly involved side. The first side was improved by decompression operation more than two months after onset. In Bell's palsy, against the other reports, the degree of palsy firstly involved side was not always severer than secondly side. In leukemia, the relapse of the leukemia was discovered by the facial palsy. And the palsy was cured by the treatment of leukemia. Metastatic adenocarcinoma in left cerebello-pontine angle cause the facial palsy of not only the left side but also the rigfht side which was previously misdiagnosed as Bell's palsy. The cause of the palsy of the right side turned out to be meningeal carcinomatosis.
