N2  - A 27-year-old man presented simultaneous bilateral facial paralysis following an abnormal sense of taste. His illness was diagnosed as bilateral simultaneous Bell's palsy, because there was no evidence of systemic diseases. About 5 weeks after the onset he showed a complete and bilateral recovery with conservative treatment. Bilateral facial nerve paralysis is infrequent, and its completely simultaneous onset, such as in this case, was thought to be extremely rare.
