N2  - Twenty six patients with parotid tumor are reported. The significance of utilization of evoked EMG is discussed. Abnormal response in evoked EMG without facial weakness - preparalytic condition - was found in 4 patients; these were 2 patients with malignant mixed tumors and 2 with benign mixed tumors. Exposure of the facial nerve was required in 3 of the 4. Postoperative facial paralysis was found in only 1 patient with benign mixed tumor among the 4. Facial weakness was not found in any of the 26 patients before surgical treatment. Evoked EMG for parotid tumors before surgical treatment was useful in early diagnosis of the damage of the facial nerve and for estimation of the condition around the facial nerve.
