N2  - We report the case of a man with chronic suppurative otitis media caused by M. tuberculosis that was associated with deafness, diplopia, facial nerve palsy, and debilitating ataxia. These symptoms were only partially responsive to medical therapy. In addition, the patient had two intracranial mass lesions, probably resulting from hematogenous dissemination of M. tuberculosis.
