N2  - Data from self-perceptions of 55 female facial aesthetic surgery patients have been combined to show a general composite picture. Personal demographic data, life circumstances, and general attitudes are presented. Patients' motivations for surgery and expectations (both aesthetic result and resulting life changes) have been examined. Patient opinions of how their desires were met are included. The data show the patients' reactions to pre- and postoperative information, self-care instructions, and general staff management. Prominent psychological processes in patients presenting for these surgeries are revealed.
