N2  - This update presents the highlights of what has been published in the last 10 years regarding disorders of the facial nerve which continue to be a subject full of controversies as well as unsolved problems. A review is made of the various aspects of Bell's palsy including medical and surgical treatment and animal experimental research. Nerve repair is discussed as regards timing, end to end nerve repair and epineurial and interfascicular repair. Up to date information is also provided about nerve and muscle biopsy as well as the problem as it presents in children. The subject of reanimation surgery is also reviewed.
