N2  - Twenty-five patients with unilateral long established facial paralysis had their facial disability reconstructed in a two-stage procedure by cross facial grafting and gracillis muscle transfer. There has been one complete failure, one partial failure and three are too early to evaluate, and of the remaining 21 all have functional muscle movement, eight of which move independently of the opposite normal side which is the source of reinnervation.
