N2  - A significant proportion of patients with peripheral facial paralysis are left with residual signs. They have to learn to live with a changed appearance: a more or less lopsided face and frequently also impaired capacities of expression. On the assumption that the ability to cope with these permanent changes might be improved by discussion of problems and experiences with fellow sufferers, we have established an experimental group of fellow sufferers in cooperation with the patients. Procedures in this group are described. The question to what such groups owe their effectivity is considered in the discussion.
