N2  - A case of intraocular gnathostomiasis in a 22-year-old Malaysian university student is reported. This case is unique in its photographic demonstration of the parasite attached to a retinal vessel in the patient's left eye. The worm was removed by vitrectomy and identified as the third larval stage of Gnathostoma spinigerum. Removal of the parasite may have been lifesaving in view of the longevity of the worm in the human host and the potential for central nervous system involvement.
