N2  - In a review of the literature, the possible uses of ACTH and glucocorticoids in neurology are discussed. ACTH is indicated particularly in pseudoparalytic myasthenia gravis, whereas it can be recommended only with due reservations in acute episodes of multiple sclerosis, in cerebral edema and in propulsive petit-mal. Glucocorticoids are used predominantly in the treatment of pseudo-paralytic myasthenia gravis, dermatomyositis, polyneuropathies that are part of collagen diseases, temporal arteritis, rheumatic polymyalgia, the Tolosa-Hunt syndrome, tuberculous meningitis, cerebral edema and neurosarcoidosis.
