N2  - To restore facial symmetry in cases of paralyzed lower lip, the authors have followed the selective neurectomy procedure developed for the lower lip, by Marino, and Marino and Alurralde. After cadaveric dissections carried out on 10 facial halves, they demonstrated that several other interconnected branches of the facial nerve innervate the lower lip musculature. This fact led them not to limit the operation to the sectioning of the proximal marginalis mandibularis, but to include in the neurectomy these peripheral branches also. As a result of the more extensive resection of motor nerves the return of movement to the denervated muscles can be avoided.
