N2  - Peripheral facial paralysis is a very frequent affection. 400 cases have been treated in the E.N.T. Department of Bordeaux between 1973 and 1979. The localization of the facial nerve in the temporal bone means its diagnosis and treatment belong to the E.N.T. field. For diagnosis we have been able to pinpoint the importance of the lesions of the nerve and their localization. The muscular test, clearly quantified and easy to practise, is added to exploration of the function of other facial nerve branches (tear-test, gustametry, stapedius reflex study). The electric test gives us a prognosis. A best evaluation of facial paralysis gives fewer surgical indications, but is more precise. Facial paralysis requires immediate diagnosis and treatment. The aim is to eliminate sequellae of the movements of the face, so important in social intercourse.
