N2  - An embryonal rhabdomyosarcoma of the middle ear occurring in a child is described. The disease history showed an acute process in the middle ear accompanied by early seventh nerve paralysis. The external auditory canal was filled with a rapidly growing polypoid mass. Surgical treatment was limited and provided adequate biopsy material. Treatment consisted of multiple-drug chemotherapy and radiation therapy followed by maintenance chemotherapy. The facial nerve paralysis resolved and the patient has remained free of disease one year after treatment was started.
