N2  - Electrophysiological methods of examination of the facial nerve provide information concerning the degree of nerve damage and the progress c.q. arrest of instituted treatment; they may also be used to assess therapeutic results of peripheral facial paresis. Since 1975, the ORL Clinic of the University of Halle in addition to the traditional methods of functional and topical diagnosis applies electroneuronogaphy to study facial nerve function. So far it has been carried out in 197 patients. Findings prove electroneuronography to be an adequate method for objective determination of facial nerve function. It constitutes a valuable addition to traditional methods of examination, especially in questions of the therapeutic consequences in recent peripheral facial paresis.
