N2  - Leukaemic infiltration of the petrous temporal bone is uncommon but with improved remission rates longer survival in leukemia isolated sites of relapse can be expected more frequently. Mastoid chloroma requires treatment with chemotherapy and radiotherapy. Wide-field mastoidectomy and facial nerve decompression are contraindicated.
