N2  - A young woman presented with flaccid quadraparesis, a right infranuclear facial palsy and limb areflexia following a two-day history of severe streptococcal pharyngitis. She was found to have cerebellar ataxia in the upper limbs with normal deep sensation. Bilateral papilloedema developed a year later during her third relapse. Treatment with high dose of prednisolone on an alternate day regimen basis induced a long lasting remission including improvement of her cerebellar deficit. The mechanism of cerebellar involvement and the pathogenesis of her papilloedema were uncertain. This is in keeping with the views previously expressed by earlier authors.
