N2  - Leprous facial paralysis appears more frequently in Iran than in other countries. The damaged branch is more often the upper one inducing lagophthalmos and is sometimes associated with a trigeminal anesthesia. The ocular risk is great. When the lower branch is afflicted, it gives an anesthetic deformity and speaking difficulty. As a consequence, surgical treatment is necessary and directed; against lagophthalmos, with static or dynamic methods, against the ptosis of commissura labiorum with several techniques available.
