N2  - Orbicularis oculi responses evoked by supraorbital and facial nerve stimulation were studied in 24 patients with unilateral hemispheral lesions. The direct facial motor response was only altered on the involved side and only in cases of central facial palsy. This influence was more expressed on the involved side. On the basis of changes in latency, duration, amplitude values and in habituation of late responses the effect of hemispheral lesions must be taken for depressing type either on R1 or R2 responses. These data suggest an exteroceptive character of both responses.
