N2  - A study of the 20 cases shows results which are, on the whole, disappointing, although we always obtained active movement of the eyelids. There can be no doubt that ancillary simple procedures (section of the mentalis, frontal myomectomy, tension of the musculo-aponeurotic system and skin elements, or reconstructive surgery of the eyelid) make a major contribution to the symmetry of the face and the protection of the cornea. In the light of these results, we have abandoned transfacial anastomoses in favour of hypoglossal facial nerve anastomosis associated with simple procedures to improve symmetry. Comparative analysis of the results of the two techniques will show which procedure provides the better rehabilitation.
