N2  - The authors present a case of unilateral Moebius syndrome associated with Poland abnormality in a 25-year woman. The patient had a complete left peripheral facial paralysis. In addition, there was microdactyly, syndactyly of the left hand, absence of the pectoralis major, of the mammary gland and nipple adding up to a Poland syndrome. Surgery was envisaged with the aim of performing a hypoglossofacial anastomosis. Operation revealed muscles of normal appearance with a somewhat thin digastric and total absence of the facial nerve both at the point of its emergence through the stylomastoid foramen as well as in the parotid.
