N2  - An adult male patient suffered a partial palsy of the right mandibular branch of the facial nerve resulting from anesthesia under mask. A good airway is usually achieved by tight digital compression around the angle of the mandibulae. As in this case, if continuous bilateral digital pressure is applied on the angle of the jaw to provide a clear airway, the facial nerve is in danger of being pinched between the fingers and the ascending ramus of the mandibulae. To avoid this risk to the nerve, the angle of the mandibulae should be held correctly and the two areas, behind the ramus or above the inferior border of the mandibulae where the mandibular branch is distributed, should not be compressed.
