N2  - In treatment of Bell's palsy, 42 patients were treated with steroid hormone and 45 without steroid hormone. About 80% of the patients showed complete recovery; recovery rates were not comparable between groups. However, the palsy of patients undergoing steroid therapy returned to normal earlier than those without steroid therapy. The patients with positive VZV skin test showed better recovery than negative ones. It seems that VZV skin test becomes one of the parameters to show whether paralysis recovers well or not.
