N2  - The treatment of the facial palsy never reestablished the symetry and harmony of a normal face. The best results are obtained in young patients during the two first years following the paralysis. The authors distinguish two main groups of facial palsies: with trophic and recuperable musculature, and with atrophic and irrecuperable musculature. They review and analyse the different surgical techniques to be applied primarily, and the secondary palliative corrections which are necessary in most of the cases. They have to be realized in agreement with the patient according to the need and desire.
