N2  - Treatment of Bell's palsy by intensive galvanic stimulation and by decompression in the second or third week after onset, has not been proved to lead to better recovery. Whether earlier surgical intervention would produced better results remains to be seen and depends on the possibility of making a fool-proof and very early prognosis, which in our opinion is not yet possible. Prednisone is now as popular as electrotherapy was a generation ago, but on equally slender grounds.
