N2  - A report is presented of Primary Epidermoid Carcinoma of the parotid gland in an 81 year old man. The tumor is firm, 6 x 4 x 3 cm, fixed to the underlying structures, not sensitive, and appeared 3 months before and is causing a total facial nerve paralysis. There are no palpable lymph nodes. Apart from a cyst of the Kidney, the complete physical and biological examination is normal. A radical parotidectomy is done, followed by a 6.000 R Cobalttherapy. Treatment was later on completed by a corner of mouth suspension. After 10 months the patient is well. Primary epidermoid carcinoma of the parotid gland is rare: between 0,1% and 1,5% of all parotid tumors. Mucoepidermoid carcinoma or metastatic squamous carcinoma must be ruled out.
