N2  - A number of complications occurring during and after stapedial operations for otosclerosis are dealt with. More particularly, a patient with bilateral dehiscence of the facial nerve canal is studied, where following blood aspiration, paresis of the facial nerve situated just beneath the mucosa developed. The other patients discussed include: a second case with canal dehiscence, a case with acute otitis and n. facialis paresis, and a case with acute otitis and labyrinthitis in whom the sense of hearing failed to recover. It is strongly recommended to carry out the operative intervention under conditions of exceptional acepsis. Also, it is mandatory to perform a careful prophylactical examination of the upper airways before the operation.
