N2  - Practicing logical postoperative treatment requires knowledge about the processes involved in nerve regeneration, which are briefly dealt with. However, it is the opinion of the authors that greater attention should be given to the reaction of the denervated musculature. For effective electrotherapy, recent findings from animal experiments on changes at the membrane of the muscle fiber seem to be of paramount importance, at least from a theoretical point of view. Practical consequences result from these findings, but the physiological behavior of the mimetic muscles is different from that of the skeletal muscles, and the usefulness of electrotherapy on facial musculature is still controversial.
