N2  - Before Thompson's treatment of facial paralysis corrective surgery of these lesions had followed indirect and not direct methods. The re-acquisition of the contracting capacity of a denervated muscle, once put in contact with a normal muscle, has marked a decisive and effective turn in paralysis. The uniting of Thompson's method with nervous by-pass from the normal side to the paralyzed side by neuro-surgical method according to Anderl, is opening up continously growing possibilities of recovery for paralyzed facial muscles. Of course, this method is not possible without an adequate staff with micro-surgical experience. The authors present their patients' case histories treated with Thompson's method.
