N2  - Surgical treatment was conducted in 25 patients with glomus tumours of the pyramid (5), cystic arachnoiditis of the cerebellopontile angle (5), neurinoma of the auditory nerve (4), paralysis of the facial nerve in fracture of the pyramid (4), choleastoma of the cereballopontile angle (1), gun shot wound of the pyramid (1), and purulent labyrinthitis (1). The pathological focus was approached transpyramidally (13), suprapyramidally (4), and by the combined method (4). In the choice of the method, approach localization and dissemination of the process, as well as the state of the auditory function and condition of the facial nerve were taken into consideration. No lethal outcome followed these operations.
