N2  - During the period from March 1974 through August 1978 we treated 21 cases of Bell's palsy by electric acupuncture. Diagnosis was based on neurological examination. The method of treatment is described in detail. Acupuncture points used were located on the afflicted side. Good results were seen in 14 cases (66.67%), 5 cases showed considerable improvement (23.80%), and 2 cases were considered as failure (9.53%). Electric acupuncture is recommended as the method of first choice for the successful treatment of Bell's palsy.
