N2  - A report is presented of personal experience with prednisone treatment of 76 patients with severe acute idiopathic facial paralysis (Bell's palsy). The indication for treatment is total or subtotal loss of the motor function, determined by clinical examination. The author advocates treatment of selected patients at an early stage, at the last 5 to 7 days after the diagnosis.
