N2  - A case of chronic granulomatous disease is reported. A 1.8 year old boy had suffered from recurrent infections such as cervical lymphadenitis, eczematous dermatitis and perianal abscess in his newborn period. Later he developed left facial palsy, otitis media and intermittent fever. Otoscopic examination revealed a granulomatous mass in the left external auditory meatus, and x-ray showed a diffuse shadow in the left mastoid. Simple mastoidectomy was performed on May 26, 1978. Under intensive postoperative care, the patient has been free from fever and local infection.
