N2  - Three cases of tuberculous otitis media are reported. In two adult cases, vertigo, facial palsy and severe hearing impairment appeared three months after the onset. The latter two symptoms persisted in spite of the surgical and medical treatment. In a child case, an early diagnosis prevented the patient from any sequelae. Necrotic changes of the ear drum, external auditory canal or tympanic cavity were characteristic in all these cases. It seems important, in case of necrotic otitis media, to take tuberculosis into consideration.
