N2  - Amyotrophic lateral sclerosis, progressive bulbar paralysis and spinal progressive muscular atrophy should be regarded as one nosological unit. They are the most frequent manifestation types of degenerative diseases of the pyramidal motor system leading to gradually progressive atrophic and/or spastic paralyses. The cause is not known; occasional familial occurrence suggests genetic determination. The diagnosis has to be made on clinical grounds. No treatment is known. The prognosis is unfavorable; a few special hereditary types run a relatively benign course.
