N2  - A partial decompression of the facial nerve consists in fenestration of its tympanal part (area from projection of incus long process to pyramidal process) with epineural membrane dissection. The patients were operated on 45-70 days from the beginning of disease (after the failure of conservative therapy) in the presence of deep paralysis without amelioration. A parallelism between facial nerve and chorda tympani states was marked: in hyperemia and edema of the latter the analogous changes are seen in the facial nerve. In all patients who had undergone surgery the positive results were obtained. The authors consider that surgery should be performed early.
