N2  - Facio-facial anastomosis represents an important therapeutic contribution to the difficult treatment of peripheral facial paralyses. Though difficult to perform, this procedure has been rendered possible by the considerable progress brought by the operative microscope and the microsurgical techniques; it opens up a new way for these patients. However, only experience and the practice of this new surgical method will determine its value in the future.
