N2  - Methods of treatment of 200 patients suffering from acute neuritis of the facial nerve occurring in 42 patients with acute otitis media and in 158 patients with chronic otitis media are reported. Paracenthesis and conservative treatment of acute otitis media from the first day of the nerve affection, and complex surgical (operation on the ear and partial decompression of the facial nerve) and conservative treatment of chronic purulent otitis media are recommended. The results of treatment are briefly analyzed. Of 200 patients, complete restoration of the facial nerve function was achieved in 174 cases. The cosmetic effect was good in 6, and satisfactory - in 20 cases.
