N2  - Two cases of acoustic neurinoma with an atypical onset are described. The first case manifested itself with facial paralysis without discernible cause; surgical decompression of the facial nerve was attempted. The second patient presented sudden deafness after an injury to the cervical spine, followed by a syndrome suggestive of vertebrobasilar insufficiency. Arteriography revealed vascular displacement of tumoral origin. It is emphasized that transorbital radiography should be carried out in every case of unilateral inner-ear deafness.
