N2  - A rare form of Wegener's granulomatosis is reported by the authors. The disease began in the form of acute otitis, and the classic form developed after a bilateral complete hearing defect, peripheral vestibular lesion, and facial paresis. The patient died. Attention is called by the authors to the importance of early diagnosis, since by early adequate treatment (steroids and cytostatic drugs) remission may be obtained.
