N2  - In a statistical group of 300 patients with peripheral paralysis of facial nerve from the total of 20,749 hospitalized patients of the Otolaryngological Clinic of Medical Academy in Erfurt (GDR), the subjects are divided into 7 groups according to the cause of the disease. A detailed examination indicated only 29% of etiologically obscure cases. The introduced therapy including surgical therapy in indicated cases resulted in a complete regression in 75% of cases, improvement in 17%, while only 8% of patients were not influenced by the treatment. The authors are of the opinion that a timely diagnosis of the etiological factors of the disease, as well as a timely, whenever possible, causal therapy including surgery, would enable to decrease the percentage of unsatisfactory therapeutic results.
