N2  - In the light of one case of postembolisation lower motor neurone facial paralysis, it was felt to be of interest to draw attention to the possible role played by the middle meningeal artery: - in the etiogenesis of certain peripheral problems affecting the facial nerve during embolisation of the medial maxillary ; in the indirect recognition of a dangerous anatomical distribution. The easy identification of its endocrine branch and of the stylo-mastoid artery should reveal the mode of arterial distribution of the facial nerve: and hence to assess the risks run by patients during embolisation, according to the territory and the equipment.
