N2  - In the ENT clinic of the University of Halle in the period 1966 to 1976, 780 patients with peripheral facialis paresis could be treated conservatively or surgically. The causes of the condition for which the patients came for treatment were otogenic damage, traumatism, iatrogenic causes and, in the majority of cases, the so-called idiopathic pareses. An account is given of a programme of examinations of the functional and topical diagnosis, that proved its value in particular in the indication of the therapy of choice. The functional results have, it is true, greatly improved, but the number of so-called defective cures is too high, in the opinion of the authors, and is avoidable. Emphasis is laid on the examinations that are available for the surgical indication.
