N2  - Peripheral facial nerve paresis produces a certain amount of dismay and anxiety not so much in its threat to health but more for its severe cosmetic impact. In spite of the numerous therapeutic approaches to this frequently occurring nerve injury, many questions about these different approaches have sofar remained unanswered. Narrowly connected with this is the selection of necessary diagnostic measures from a large number of possible measures. Based on experiences gained with 446 patients who were examined electrodiagnostically, practical procedures for diagnosis and therapy are outlined.
