N2  - The use of kinesitherapy to treat peripheral facial paralysis is still an infrequent procedure. All types of this condition, however, can be rehabilitated, without, of course, prejudicing surgical decompression at a later date. These include facial paralysis due to cold, trauma, ear diseases, and parotidectomy. Muscle reactions have to be tested before starting treatment. The therapeutic procedures used must follow a precise pattern: application of heat, electrical stimulation under strictly defined conditions, passive and active kinesitherapy. About one hundred patients have been treated with these different methods over the last few years, and the authors report excellent results.
