N2  - A 14-year-old boy with a very rapid impairment of vision leading to complete blindness within less than 24 h is presented. Edema of discs, upward gaze palsy, unreactive pupils, left hemiparesis and central facial nerve palsy were the main clinical features. Under steroid treatment the hemiparesis and facial nerve palsy gradually disappeared and an impressive recovery of visual function was observed. The possible causes and the differential diagnosis of sudden blindness in childhood are discussed.
