N2  - The authors draw three conclusions from their experience, bearing in mind the fact that they have never used the middle fossa approach except in cases of fracture involving the first portion of VII. The fact that tomography is often unsatisfactory, a number of fracture lines being invisible on the X-ray. The importance of enlarged endaural and transmeatal approach which gives an excellent view of the nerve and ossicular chain so that the necessary surgery can be carried out at leisure. Conservation of the sulcus allows return to a strictly normal anatomical appearance once the tympanomeatal flap has been replaced in position. Above all, a point which seems fundamental to the authors, operations on the VIIth nerve should be undertaken before the sixth week.
