N2  - If the diagnosis of peripheral facial palsy is relatively easy thanks to the clinical and electrophysiological data and to the functional tests, the prognosis of a clinical facial palsy is more difficult to establish. Taking into account their personal experiments and the data in the literature, the authors describe the means which allow the formulation of prognosis on which depends the treatment (medical or surgical). They have tried to establish a well defined program which will be used later as a basis for a longitudinal study realized in common by neurologists, otorhinolaryngologists and neurophysiologists.
