N2  - Facial spasm is not so rare in Japan, but the etiology and treatment are not established. Several treatments (facial nerve block by alcohol injection, neurotomy, drug therapy and stellate ganglion block) have been tried. Wakasugi's physical block method, facial nerve block by needle insertion, is the most popular one. However, the technique is rather difficult for us and the result is not constant. Moreover we sometimes experienced that Bell's palsy was prolonged, and dizziness or inner ear disturbance was complained about. According to this technique the peripheral nerve branch of the facial nerve is found by electric stimulator under neurolept analgesia and a small amount of pure alcohol (usually 0.1 ~ 0.2 nl) is injected.
