N2  - Transposition of a temporal muscle flap according to the principles laid down by Lexer and Schmid has been suggested by the authors for the treatment of long-standing upper facial palsy. But here a lower-based pedicled flap has been used by the authors. In order to maintain innervation of the flap, it appears mandatory to separate the latter at the subperiosteal level, from above downwards, up to the perpendicular on the medial portion of the zygomatic process. Finally, emphasis is laid on the necessity to take extremely accurate landmarks prior to lateral orbitotomy, otherwise closing of the eyelids will be unsatisfactory.
