N2  - A report on a case of peripheral paralysis of the right side of the larynx in a 34 yr old male who became completely aphonic following a grippal infection. After 3 wk of conventional treatment by a well known specialist, he underwent acupuncture treatment. After 4 mth the voice was again normal; however laryngoscopy showed a completely normal larynx only 7 mth after the illness. The loci used and the reasons for their selection are discussed in detail. The second case was a 62 yr old male with facial paralysis. This patient underwent acupuncture treatment shortly after he was stricken. After 6 days distinct improvement was seen; he was completely healed after 2 mth. The loci and the reasons for their selection are discussed. The cases are compared.
