N2  - Pheripheral facial paralysis not only leads to disfigurement of the face but can also cause complications in the region of the eyes. In addition to the causative treatment of the paralysis, a few temporary measures may be of great practical value for the patient. These measures divided into those which improve appearance and those which are intended to protect the eye are described.
