N2  - The paper deals with trophic disorders of the buccal mucosa in 30 patients with Bell's paralysis. The character of the changes found was judged by the results of an examination of the mucosa and chemical and histochemical studies of the bioptate, obtained by aspirational biopsy. The examinations demonstrated trophic disorders in the buccal mucosa which were testified to by a slight edema and enzymatic-metabolic disorders in the form of increased activity of the acid and alkaline phosphatase as well as asparagine and alanine aminotransferase. These changes to a certain extent confirm the existence of vegetative filaments in the facial nerve, an affection of which leads to metabolic-trophic changes. Such data should be taken into consideration in an attempt to explain the mechanisms of distrophic processes and may be utilized as some indices in the judgement of the dynamics in the process of treatment.
