N2  - The rarity of giant cell tumors of the sphenoid bone has been emphasized by various authors. Giant cell tumors are, in general, very uncommon in the head and, when they occur, they tend to show predilection for the mandible and the maxilla. The case reported is the 16th so far published in the English language literature. It occurred in the sphenoid bone in a man of 25. Besides the familial presentation with headaches, ocular manifestations, and upper cranial nerve lesions, this case showed previously undescribed features such as grand mal seizures, hemiparesis with facial palsy and dural extension. The reported high incidence in females is questioned. Histologically, the tumor showed some cartilage.
