N2  - The treatment of complete facial paralyses until recently was rendered difficult by the absence of an electrodiagnostic method of examination that gives reliable prognostic pointers at an early stage. This gap has now been closed by neuronography. The sum of the action potentials (SAP) is a direct measure of the number of muscle fibers set into action by the nerves. Consequently, the lowering of the amplitude in comparison with the SAP of the healthy side corresponds to the number of degenerated nerve fibers. Now it is possible between the 7th and 10th days after the onset of the paralysis to obtain a reliable prognosis and indications for the essential treatment (further conservative treatment, or decompression of the facialis.
