N2  - 8 cases of cancer of the middle ear and the deep external auditory meatus are reported. Facial palsy is an important initial symptom for an early diagnosis but it is at times difficult to differentiate the cancer from the chronic middle ear inflammation. Radical ear operation or regional resection of the temporal bone combined with radio- and chemo-therapy were applied for treatment of 6 cases; 2 cases of which are still surviving over the period of 5 yr after the treatments.
