N2  - A case of multiple cranial nerve paralysis in a 48-yr-old male patient is reported. The patient suffered peripheral facial palsy of the right side which was followed by a complicated manifestation of progressive clinical symptoms. The patient diet 5 mth later. There was no abnormal finding in the examination of the cerebrospinal fluid nor in the X-ray examination of the chest; final diagnosis was clinically undetermined. However, the postmortem examination showed metastasis of the primaru lung cancer to the pia-arachnoid of the brain forming a silent phase of small cell anaplastic carcinoma. The final diagnosis was considered as diffuse metastatic leptomeningeal carcinoma.
