N2  - Three cases of facial nerve neuroma which orginated from the vertical portion of the facial nerve are reported. All three cases complained of facial nerve spasm followed by facial nerve palsy. In making a diagnosis of the facial nerve tumor, it is essential to note the presence of isolated twitching in orbicularis oris muscle and slowly progressive facial nerve weakness which follows facial spasm. Particularly when no abnormalities are found through various examinations inclusive of polytomography, the presence of facial nerve neuroma should be suspected; a careful follow-up should be performed.
