N2  - In this paper we present our experience with 32 cricomyotomies of the cricopharyngeal muscle in three groups of patients: the first consisting of patients with a pharyngeal dysphagia due to a neuromotor disorder, the second and larger one made up by patients who had undergone horizontal supraglotic laryngectomies and the third by those cases in which the myotomy was performed in the same surgical operation as the laryngectomy. In all of these, the results may be considered to be very good especially in those patients who previously had to undergo laryngeal surgery.
