N2  - Using Thompson's methods, free muscle grafts were performed on 6 cases of facial palsy. Those cases were followed up from 10 months to 18 months after operation. The effects of the grafts were analyzed as to the eyelid movement and mouth deviation. Some showed good eyelid movement and considerable improvement of deviated mouth, but this improvement was nullified when patients smiled. Thus it appears that other devices should be considered.
