N2  - A man, aged 66, suffered a malignant tumor of the parotid gland. Backache, pains in the arms and the elbows were the first manifestation of the symptoms and the parotid gland swelling appeared 3 months thereafter. This was followed by a facial nerve paralysis 20 days later. Tc(99m) and 67Ga-scannings were applied to the whole body. The parotid tumor was hypoactive to Tc(99m) and hyperactive towards 67Ga; these appear to be the most characteristic findings in the case of malignant tumors. There were, however, abnormal accumulations of Tc(99m) and 67Ga in the metastasis of the cervical vertebra. Histologic examination revealed the growth to be an adenocarcinoma. The patient was treated by administration of anticancer drug therapy and irradiation but he died a year later from metastatic pulmonary involvements.
