N2  - Microscopic trans-facial or facio-facial anastomosis is a technique that is promising in the treatment of peripheral facial paralyses - even old ones considered as incurable by other therapeutic measures. Its principal advantage is that it is a very fine approach to the physiological function of the facial nerve. Obviously it calls for familiarity with surgery under the microscope. It must be emphasized that it is not a risky method and in no way mortgages the future, because, in case of failure, muscular transplantation or cosmetic cutaneous surgery is still possible. The author considers that its indications will become wider in the future.
