N2  - The authors' experience leads them to believe that if the 7th nerve is anatomically intact after removal of a cerebellopontine angle tumor, facial motor recovery is to be expected, even in the presence of a complete facial palsy postoperatively. One may, however, have to wait as long as 12 mth for clinical signs of recovery. Recovery is likely to be better than that provided by anastomosis from another cranial nerve. The authors would recommend, therefore, that under these circumstances, at least 1 yr be allowed for spontaneous recovery. If some cosmetic procedure is required, perhaps a plastic operation rather than nerve anastomosis would be preferred.
