N2  - In the time period from 1945 to 1974 250 patients were treated for diffuse otitis interna developing as a consequence of chronic otitis media. The material was analyzed and clinical manifestations, symptomatology, treatment and early and late therapeutic results are reported. Besides labyrinthine disturbances other coexistent complications were assessed: 37 cases of facial nerve damage, 80 cases of extralabyrinthine intracranial complications situated extradurally and subdurally (granulomas and extradural abscesses of the middle and posterior cranial fossa, suppurating sigmoid sinus thrombi, purulent meningitis, cerebral and cerebellar abscesses) and 68 cases of labyrinth mediated (complicated diffuse otitis interna) intracranial complications: extradural abscesses, purulent meningitis and cerebellar abscesses.
