N2  - In acute leukemia, otological and otoneurological symptoms are frequently observed. In addition, patients with chronic lymphedema of the upper respiratory tract may have leukemic infiltration of the mucous membranes. Examples are given of the symptoms produced by leukemic infiltation of the various anatomical regions. Therapy is discussed from an interdisciplinary point of view. The first symptoms often occur in the ENT region and the author provides evidence from his own observations of symptoms such as acute otitis media, facial pareses, and acute dyspnea due to leucotic tonsillar hyperplasia or due to laryngeal infiltration. (12 references).
