N2  - The authors describe a method of plastic operation applied in unilateral facial hypoplasia following facial nerve palsy. The disturbed symmetry of the face was corrected by separating the hypoplastic malar bone with a chisel and shifting it anteriorly. At the same time the sagging angle of the mouth was drawn up by means of a bundle of fibers and temporal muscle fascia. The operation improved greatly the appearance of the patient.
