N2  - A seven year old child with a sudden onset left facial paralysis of supranuclear type, associated with left arm monoplegia, is described. E.E.G., brain scan and carotid arteriography reveal a tumoral pattern in the right temporo frontal region. Surgery disclosed a right frontal hematoma with a parasitic clump in its wall, leading to the identification of a grade II Hypoderma bovis maggot. This is the third reported case of intracerebral myiasis and emphasis must be given to its very unusual location and biological diagnosis.
