N2  - A rare case of linear scleroderma beginning with peripheral facial paralysis is reported. The authors' observations point to both immuno allergic origin and origin in the nervous system. This rare disease with neural symptoms necessitated surgical exposure of the facial nerve and the performance of fractional PEG; and initially caused difficulties in diagnosis. However, these experiences are valuable contributions to medical knowledge of the causes leading to peripheric facial paresis.
