N2  - The cerebral metastases of primary tumors often cause diagnostic difficulties. The frequency and the symptoms of the malignant tumors leading to cerebral metastases as well as the difficulties of their diagnosis are analysed. 6 months after surgical intervention, performed because of carcinoma of the mamma, facial paralysis on the right side, and 2 months later seropurulent otitis on the same side and meningitis developed, necessitating a surgical approach. Neurosurgical consultation could not unequivocally clear the presence of cerebral abscess or cerebral metastasis. The latter was verified only during the post mortem examination.
