N2  - Malignant external otitis which has a very severe prognosis has been described as being related to diabetes in old age. The authors present a case with malignant external otitis which occurred in a 10 yr old girl. The external otitis which appeared at first on the left side was accompanied on this side by a facial paralysis; 6 mth later, on the right, a malignant external otitis was found without facial palsy. Furthermore, this girl was affected by a diabetes insipidus for which no hypophysial or renal cause was found. After reviewing the literature, the authors discuss the clinical aspects and treatment of this case.
