N2  - The authors have made a review of the Melkersson Rosenthal syndrome and a new case is reported. The diagnosis of our patient was based on the recurrent facial nerve palsy, furrowed tongue, and the history of episodic lip and facial swelling accompanied by hemicranial pain. This is a syndrome without evident etiology. It is chronic and has not responded to treatment. Although it is futile to draw conclusions from one case, perhaps this syndrome is due to an autonomous nervous system defect.
