N2  - This paper reports on epithelial tumors arising primarily in the major and minor salivary glands. The purpose of this presentation is to summarize the experience with salivary gland tumors on the basis of approx. 3000 salivary gland tumors as well as a review of the literature to date. The tumors are classified according to the classification recommended by the WHO in 1972. The incidence, location, symptomatology, grade of malignancy and treatment of the different tumor types in this classification are reviewed. Diagnostic procedures are discussed and a scheme for surgical treatment and radiotherapy of the different types of salivary gland tumors is proposed.
