N2  - A new method is described for the correction of paralysis of the elevator muscles of the angle of the mouth in cases of unilateral facial paresis, by transplanting skeletal muscle as a free graft together with its motor nerve of supply, the latter being anastomosed to normal filaments of the facial nerve on the uninvolved side of the face, using microsurgical techniques. The results in twelve patients treated over a period of one year, are encouraging and are being given continuing trial. The late results of free autogenous skeletal muscle grafts in restoring movement to the eyelids and mouth regions in 103 cases of unilateral facial paralysis, involving 157 grafts, are presented.
