N2  - 47 cases of Bell's palsy and viral facial nerve paralysis have been lengthily studied on an analytical and functional basis. An important number of these cases corresponded to serious forms seen right away or lately. The importance of analytical evaluation and electric and functional explorations is underlined. Repeated, they may clarify the evolutive mode and sequelae, and also therapeutic indications. Residual functional problems are reviewed. The authors insist on the benefit of systematic, early and prolonged rehabilitation.
