N2  - A case of multiple sclerosis is described in a 6 yr old girl. During 5 yr, she had 7 relapses with the same typical clinical and biological findings. After a review of the literature 64 cases in children are summarized. The onset symptoms are comparable with those shown in the adults but abnormal gait, facial palsy, headache, tremors, dysarthries are much more common. In 37.5% of the cases, death appears after an acute course of less than 2 yr. The others are regressive cases, with minor neurological sequelae. Etiopathogeny and therapy are the same as in adults.
