N2  - With the transmeatal approach to the geniculate ganglion a decompression of the facial nerve is possible in cases of Bell's palsy and herpes zoster oticus when cochlear and vestibular function are intact. In the 10 patients whom we operated on since 1971 and who had a follow up period of more than 6 months, a recovery of facial function in all 3 branches of the nerve was found.
