N2  - A case of cheilitis granulomatosa in an 11 yr old boy is presented. The frequency of Melkersson Rosenthal syndrome in childhood is compiled from data in the literature. The Melkersson Rosenthal syndrome does not differ in children in its clinical and histological picture known from adults. In childhood, females are more often affected than males. The etiology of the syndrome is still unknown. Symptomatic and temporal improvement could be achieved following local injections of triamcinolone acetonide suspension.
