N2  - Peripheral facial palsy is one of the most frequent diseases of the brain nerves. On account of its localisation there are many different possibilities for its impairment. Despite detailed diagnostics the causes of a peripheral facial palsy are only discovered by operation. The references of cases in the literature and of seven personal observations show that by unsatisfactory functional restitution the conservative treatment of ischaemic facial palsies (Bell's palsy) should be taken into consideration.
