N2  - The results of chorda tympani neurotomy in the treatment of ischemic pareses of the facial nerve are reported. A relatively simple operative method for the treatment of pareses of the facial nerve, described and performed by Chouard and Blatt, was used in 55 cases since 1971. The presuppositions for this special treatment are the knowledge of the transmeatal ear surgery, a microsurgical instrumentarium and the consequent observance of the indication criteria for the treatment of ischemic pareses of the facial nerve. On average hospitalization lasts 8 days. Of the 55 patients 46 had a highly restricted function of the facial nerve before treatment, in 5 patients the function was deficient. In the after examination the condition was to be regarded as normal in 35 cases, in 11 patients the function was essentially improved and only in 9 patients this intervention had no success.
