N2  - The case of a 3-year-old female is reported whose condition was diagnosed as congenital, complete paralysis of the right facial nerve in 1962; and a short time later more specifically described as Moebius syndrome. In 1971, a circumoral fascial sling was inserted. Voluntary movement on the right side of her mouth was noted and continued to improve, making facial actions more symmetrical. This function has remained stable during a five year follow-up.
