N2  - This study was not designed to make a comparison with other soft lenses, and enthusiasm over the success rate must be tempered by remembering that the criteria for success, symptomatic relief and re epithelialization, are somewhat limited. The Plano 'T' lens did, however, perform well in achieving these specified objectives. The ease of fitting, regardless of corneal shape or size, or the presence of corneal or conjunctival irregularities, offers a distinct advantage over many other soft lenses. The tolerance was extremely good. Occasional lenses were lost, especially in patients with facial palsy, but only one serious complication arose in the whole study.
