N2  - Causes, clinical picture, diagnosis, treatment and outcome of this condition were studied in 13 boys and 8 girls aged 5 mths to 12 yrs. Causes were Bell's palsy (5 children); otitis, mastoiditis or both (9 children); malignant tumours (2 children); congenital abnormalities (2 children); trauma, herpes zoster and rheumatic fever (1 case each). Treatment was mainly surgical (14 cases) or medicinal (5 cases). Decompression is recommended when these patients fail to improve after 4 to 6 wks of conservative treatment.
