N2  - The anatomical diagnosis in these patients is reached through clinical history; physical examination (including neurological, otological and ophthalmological examination); Schirmer's test; assessment of taste in the anterior 2/3 of the tongue; tests for submaxillary and sublingual saliva. Clinical diagnosis is completed with Hilger's test; electromyography; electronystamography; audiometry; radiograms and blood sugar concentrations. Medicinal treatment includes dexamethasone, nicotinyl alcohol, diazepam and cyproheptadine. Decompression surgery is considered after the second wk of conservative treatment depending on progress.
