N2  - The major complications associated with acute suppurative disease in the ear and paranasal sinuses are discussed as well as their medical management and the indications for surgical intervention. Both rhinocerebral phycomycosis (mucormycosis) and malignant external otitis are life threatening acute infections in which surgical intervention often must accompany the medical management. The specific details of surgical treatment, which are discussed in standard textbooks, are not to be described in detail.
