N2  - After a brief survey on the anatomical peculiarities of the course followed by the facial nerve and of the structures it innervates, the authors share their experience with the methods employed in establishing the level of its injury. To this end the Schirmer's test of tear production, taste determination through electrogustometry, investigation of the secretion of saliva and audiometry are used. On the ground of the obtained data eight levels of facial nerve lesion are determined in accordance with Jepssen's scheme. A total of 32 patients with different levels of facial nerve injury were studied. Most of them were subjected to operation, and thus the results of the functional nervus facialis investigation were verified. Level diagnostics is of utmost importance in the treatment and prognosis of facial nerve injuries.
