N2  - A case of complete unilateral facial-palsy of lower motor neurone type, of two months duration, following removal of foreign body from the same ear under general anaesthesia is reported. Exploration revealed a bony spicule, as a result of fissure (fracture in the anterior wall of the bony facial canal), pressing on the facial nerve. Progressive clinical improvement as confirmed by electrical tests has followed removal of the bony spicule together with decompression of the nerve.
